CARE-EXC-0001,Care Health,Care,Annexure VI 91,1,"For the purposes of interpretation and understanding of this Policy, the Company has defined below some of the important words used in this Policy. Words not defined below are to be construed in the usual English language meaning as contained in Standard English language dictionaries. The words and expressions defined in the Insurance Act, IRDA Act, regulations notified by the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India (“Authority”) and circulars and guidelines issued by the Authority shall carry the meanings described therein. The terms and conditions, insurance coverage and exclusions, other benefits, various procedures and conditions which have been built in to the Policy are to be construed in accordance with the applicable provisions contained in the Policy.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0002,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.1,"Accident/Accidental is a sudden, unforeseen and involuntary event caused by external, visible and violent means.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0003,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.3,"AYUSH Day Care Centre means and includes Community Health Centre (CHC), Primary H e a l t h Centre (PHC), Dispensary, Clinic, Polyclinic or any such centre which is registered with the local authorities, wherever applicable, and having facilities for carrying out treatment procedures and medical or surgical/para-surgical interventions or both under the supervision of registered AYUSH Medical Practitioner (s) on day care basis without in-patient services and must comply with all the following criterion:",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0004,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.4,"Cashless Facility means a facility extended by the insurer to the Insured where the payments, of the costs of treatment undergone by the insured in accordance with the Policy terms and conditions, are directly made to the network Provider by the insurer to the extent pre-authorization is approved.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0005,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.5,Condition Precedent shall mean a Policy term or condition upon which the Insurer's liability under the Policy is conditional upon.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0006,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.6,"Congenital Anomaly refers to a condition(s) which is present since birth, and which is abnormal with reference to form, structure or position.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0007,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.8,Cumulative Bonus shall mean any increase or addition in the Sum Insured granted by the insurer without an associated increase in premium.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0008,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.9,"Day Care Centre means any institution established for day care treatment of illness and/or injuries or a medical setup with a hospital and which has been registered with the local authorities, wherever applicable, and is under the supervision of a registered and qualified medical practitioner AND must comply with all minimum criteria as under -.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0009,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.10,Day Care Treatment refers to medical treatment and/or a surgical procedure which is:,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0010,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.10,Treatment normally taken on an out-patient basis is not included in the scope of this definition.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0011,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.11,Deductible is a cost-sharing requirement under a health insurance policy that provides that the insurer will not be liable for a specified rupee amount in case of indemnity policies and for a specified number of days/ hours in case of hospital cash policies which will apply before any benefits are payable by the insurer. A deductible does not reduce the Sum Insured.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-DEF-0012,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.12,"Dental Treatment means a treatment related to teeth or structures supporting teeth including examinations, fillings (where appropriate), crowns, extractions and surgery.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0013,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.14,Domiciliary Hospitalization means medical treatment for an illness/ disease/ injury which in the normal course would require care and treatment at a Hospital but is actually taken while confined at home under any of the following circumstances:,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0014,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.15,"Emergency Care (Emergency) means management for an illness or injury which results in symptoms which occur suddenly and unexpectedly, and requires immediate care by a medical practitioner to prevent death or serious long term impairment of the insured Person's health.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-WAI-0015,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.15,which premium payment can be made to renew or continue a policy in force without loss of continuity benefits pertaining to waiting periods and coverage of pre-existing diseases. Coverage need not be available during the period for which no premium is received. The grace period for payment of the premium for all types of insurance policies shall be: fifteen days where premium payment mode is monthly and thirty days in all other cases.,WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
CARE-COV-0016,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.15,"Provided the insurers shall offer coverage during the grace period, if the premium is paid in instalments during the policy period.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-DEF-0017,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.17,"Hospital means any institution established for in-patient care and day care treatment of illness and/or injuries and which has been registered as a hospital with the local authorities under the Clinical Establishments (Registration and Regulation) Act, 2010 or under the enactments specified under the Schedule of Section 56(1) of the said Act OR complies with all minimum criteria as under:",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0018,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.18,"Hospitalization means admission in a Hospital for a minimum period of 24 consecutive 'In-patient Care' hours except for specified procedures/treatments, where such admission could be for a period of less than 24 consecutive hours.",DEFINITION,True,"Hospitalization means admission in a Hospital for a minimum period of 24 consecutive 'In-patient Care' hours except for specified procedures/treatments, where such admission could be for a period of less than 24 consecutive hours.",24 hours
CARE-DEF-0019,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.19,Illness means a sickness or a disease or a pathological condition leading to the impairment of normal physiological function and requires medical treatment.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0020,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.19(a),"Acute condition - Acute condition is a disease, illness or injury that is likely to respond quickly to treatment which aims to return the person to his or her state of health immediately before suffering the disease/ illness/ injury which leads to full recovery.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-DEF-0021,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.19(b),"Chronic condition - A chronic condition is defined as a disease, illness, or injury that has one or more of the following characteristics:",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0022,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.20,"Injury means accidental physical bodily harm excluding illness or disease solely and directly caused by external, violent and visible and evident means which is verified and certified by a Medical Practitioner.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0023,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.21,In-patient Care not applicable for Overseas Travel Insurance) means treatment for which the Insured Person has to stay in a Hospital for more than 24 hours for a covered event.,COVERAGE,False,,24 hours
CARE-DEF-0024,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.22,"Intensive Care Unit (ICU) means an identified section, ward or wing of a Hospital which is under the constant supervision of a dedicated Medical Practitioner(s), and which is specially equipped for the continuous monitoring and treatment of patients who are in a critical condition, or require life support facilities and where the level of care and supervision is considerably more sophisticated and intensive than in the ordinary and other wards.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0025,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.23,"ICU Charges or (Intensive care Unit) Charges means the amount charged by a Hospital towards ICU expenses which shall include the expenses for ICU bed, general medical support services provided to any ICU patient including monitoring devices, critical care nursing and intensivist charges.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0026,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.25,Medical Advice means any consultation or advice from a Medical Practitioner including the issue of any prescription or follow-up prescription.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0027,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.26,"Medical Expenses means those expenses that an Insured Person has necessarily and actually incurred for medical treatment on account of Illness or Accident on the advice of a Medical Practitioner, as long as these are no more than would have been payable if the Insured Person had not been insured and no more than other Hospitals or doctors in the same locality would have charged for the same medical treatment.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-DEF-0028,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.28,"Medically Necessary Treatment (not applicable for Overseas Travel Insurance) means any treatment, tests, medication, or stay in Hospital or part of a stay in Hospital which:",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-WAI-0029,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.29,"Migration means a facility provided to policyholders (including all members under family cover and group policies), to transfer the credits gained for pre-existing diseases and specific waiting periods from one health insurance policy to another with the same insurer.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
CARE-DEF-0030,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.30,"Network Provider (not applicable for Overseas Travel Insurance) means the Hospitals enlisted by an Insurer, TPA or jointly by an Insurer and TPA to provide medical services to an Insured by a Cashless Facility.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0031,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.31,Newborn baby means baby born during the Policy Period and is aged up to 90 days.,DEFINITION,False,,90 days
CARE-DEF-0032,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.32,"Non-Network means any hospital, day care centre or other provider that is not part of the network.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0033,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.33,Notification of Claim means the process of intimating a Claim to the Insurer or TPA through any of the recognized modes of communication.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-WAI-0034,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.35,"Portability means a facility provided to the health insurance policyholders (including all members under family cover), to transfer the credits gained for, pre-existing diseases and specific waiting periods from one insurer to another insurer.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
CARE-WAI-0035,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.36,"Pre-existing Disease means any condition, ailment, injury or disease:",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
CARE-WAI-0036,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.36(i),That is/ are diagnosed by a physician not more than 36 months prior to the date of commencement of the policy issued by the insurer; or.,WAITING_PERIOD,False,,36 months
CARE-WAI-0037,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.36(ii),"For which medical advice or treatment was recommended by, or received from, a physician, not more than 36 months prior to the date of commencement of the policy.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,36 months
CARE-DEF-0038,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.37,"Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses means Medical Expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days preceding the hospitalization of the Insured Person, provided that:",DEFINITION,True,"Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses means Medical Expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days preceding the hospitalization of the Insured Person, provided that:",
CARE-DEF-0039,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.38,Post-hospitalization Medical Expenses means Medical Expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days immediately after the Insured Person is discharged from the Hospital provided that:,DEFINITION,True,Post-hospitalization Medical Expenses means Medical Expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days immediately after the Insured Person is discharged from the Hospital provided that:,
CARE-DEF-0040,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.39,Qualified Nurse means a person who holds a valid registration from the Nursing Council of India or the Nursing Council of any state in India.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-WAI-0041,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.40,Reasonable and Customary Charges defines the terms on which the contract of insurance can be renewed on mutual consent with a provision of Grace Period for treating the renewal continuous for the purpose of all waiting periods.,WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
CARE-WAI-0042,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.41,Renewal defines the terms on which the contract of insurance can be renewed on mutual consent with a provision of Grace Period for treating the renewal continuous for the purpose of all waiting periods.,WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
CARE-DEF-0043,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.42,Room Rent means the amount charged by a Hospital towards Room & Boarding expenses and shall include the associated medical expenses.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0044,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.43,Subrogation (Applicable to other than Health Policies and health sections of Travel and PA policies) means the right of the Insurer to assume the rights of the Insured Person to recover expenses paid out under the Policy that may be recovered from any other source.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-DEF-0045,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.44,"Surgery/Surgical Procedure means manual and/ or operative procedure(s) required for treatment of an Illness or Injury, correction of deformities and defects, diagnosis and cure of diseases, relief from suffering and prolongation of life, performed in a Hospital or a Day Care Centre by a Medical Practitioner.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0046,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.45,"Unproven/ Experimental Treatment means a treatment including drug experimental therapy which is not based on established medical practice in India, is treatment experimental or unproven.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0047,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.46,"AYUSH treatment refers to the medical and / or hospitalization treatments given under Ayurveda, Yoga and Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha and Homeopathy systems.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0048,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.47,"Break in policy means the period of gap that occurs at the end of the existing policy term/installment premium due date, when the premium due for renewal on a given policy or installment premium due is not paid on or before the premium renewal date or grace period.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-EXC-0049,Care Health,Care,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.48,"Specific waiting period means a period up to 36 months from the commencement of a health insurance policy during which period specified diseases/treatments (except due to an accident) are not covered. On completion of the period, diseases/ treatments shall be covered provided the policy has been continuously renewed without any break.",EXCLUSION,True,Specific waiting period means a period up to 36 months from the commencement of a health insurance policy during which period specified diseases/treatments (except due to an accident) are not covered.,36 months
CARE-DEF-0050,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.1,Age means the completed age of the Insured Person as on his last birthday.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0051,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.3,Ambulance means a road vehicle operated by a licensed/ authorized service provider and equipped for the transport and paramedical treatment of the person requiring medical attention.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0052,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.4,Annexure means a document attached and marked as an Annexure to this Policy.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0053,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.5,Assistance Service Provider means the service provider specified in the Policy Schedule appointed by the Company from time to time.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-WAI-0054,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.6,"Break in Policy occurs at the end of the existing policy term, when the premium due for renewal on a given policy is not paid on or before the premium renewal date or within 30 days thereof.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
CARE-COV-0055,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.7,Claim means a demand made in accordance with the terms and conditions of the Policy for payment of the specified Benefits in respect of the Insured Person.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0056,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.8,Claimant means a person who possesses a relevant and valid Insurance Policy which is issued by the Company and is eligible to file a Claim in the event of a covered loss.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-DEF-0057,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.9,Company (also referred as We/ Us) means Care Health Insurance Limited.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0058,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.10,"Diagnosis means pathological conclusion drawn by a registered medical practitioner, supported by acceptable Clinical, radiological, histological, histo-pathological and laboratory evidence wherever applicable.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0059,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.12,"Indemnity/ Indemnify means compensating the Insured Person up to the extent of Expenses incurred, on occurrence of an event which results in a financial loss and is covered as the subject matter of the Insurance Cover.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-DEF-0060,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.13,Insured Person (Insured) means a person whose name specifically appears under Insured in the Policy Schedule and with respect to whom the premium has been received by the Company.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-EXC-0061,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.14,"Mental Illness means a substantial disorder of thinking, mood, perception, orientation or memory that grossly impairs judgment, behavior, capacity to recognize, reality or ability to meet the ordinary demands of life, mental conditions associated with the abuse of alcohol and drugs, but does not include mental retardation which is a condition of arrested or incomplete development of mind of a person, specially characterized by sub normality of intelligence.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0062,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.15,Preventive Care means any kind of treatment taken as a pro-active care measure without actual requirement or symptoms of a disease or illness.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0063,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.16,"Policy means these Policy terms and conditions and Annexures thereto, the Proposal Form, Policy Schedule and Optional Cover (if applicable) which form part of the Policy and shall be read together.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-DEF-0064,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.17,Policy Schedule means the certificate attached to and forming part of this Policy.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0065,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.18,Policyholder (also referred as You) means the person named in the Policy Schedule as the Policyholder.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0066,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.19,Policy Period means the period commencing from the Policy Period Start Date and ending on the Policy Period End Date as specified in the Policy Schedule.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0067,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.20,"Policy Period End Date means the date on which the Policy expires, as specified in the Policy Schedule.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0068,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.21,"Policy Period Start Date means the date on which the Policy commences, as specified in the Policy Schedule.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0069,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.22,Policy Year means a period of 12 consecutive months commencing from the Policy Period Start Date or any anniversary thereof.,DEFINITION,False,,12 months
CARE-DEF-0070,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.23,"Rehabilitation means assisting an Insured Person who, following a Medical Condition, requires assistance in physical, vocational, independent living and educational pursuits to restore him to the position in which he was in, prior to such medical condition occurring.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0071,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.24,Senior Citizen means any person who has completed sixty or more years of age as on the date of commencement or renewal of a health insurance policy.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0072,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.25,Single Private Room means an air conditioned room in a Hospital where a single patient is accommodated and which has an attached toilet (lavatory and bath). Such room type shall be the most basic and the most economical of all accommodations available as a Single room in that Hospital.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0073,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.26,"Sum Insured (Base Sum Insured) means the amount specified in the Policy Schedule, for which premium is paid by the Policyholder.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0074,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.27,"Third Party Administrator or TPA means any person who is licensed under the IRDA (Third Party Administrators-Health Services) Regulations, 2001 by the Authority, and is engaged, for a fee or remuneration by an Insurance Company, for the purposes of providing health services.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0075,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.28,"Total Sum Insured is the sum total of Base Sum Insured and the Sum Insured accrued as No C l a i m s Bonus and / or No Claims Bonus Super (Optional Cover) and/or Automatic R e c h a r g e a n d / o r Unlimited Automatic Recharge (Optional Cover) and/or Additional Sum Insured for Accidental Hospitalization (Optional Cover) and/or Loyalty Bonus (Optional Cover). It represents the Company's maximum, total and cumulative liability for in respect of the Insured Person for any and all Claims incurred during the Policy Year. If the Policy Period is more than 12 months, then it is clarified that the Sum Insured shall be applied separately for each Policy Year in the Policy Period.",COVERAGE,False,,12 months
CARE-DEF-0076,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.29,Associate Medical Expenses means those Medical Expenses as listed below which vary in accordance with the Room Rent or Room Category applicable in a Hospital:,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0077,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.29,"The following definitions are redefined which supersedes those respective definitions mentioned above, for Benefits and Optional Covers effective out of India:",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-DEF-0078,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.30,Medical Practitioner means a person who holds a valid registration issued by the Medical Council/ Statutory Regulatory Authority for Medical Education in that Country and is thereby entitled to practice medicine within its jurisdiction; and is acting within the scope and jurisdiction of license.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0079,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.31,Qualified Nurse means a person who holds a valid registration issued by the Nursing Council/ Statutory Regulatory Authority for Medical Education in that Country and thereby entitled to render Nursing Care within the scope and jurisdiction of license.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0080,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.32,"Unproven/ Experimental Treatment means a treatment including drug experimental therapy which is not based on established medical practice, is treatment experimental or unproven.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0081,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3,GENERAL CONDITIONS APPLICABLE TO ALL BENEFITS AND OPTIONAL COVERS:,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0082,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(a),"Benefits / Optional Covers (if opted) shall be available to the Insured Person, only if the particular Benefit / Optional Cover is specifically mentioned in the Policy Schedule.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0083,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(b),"Admissibility of a Claim under Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses) is a pre-condition to the admission of a Claim under Benefit 2 (Pre Hospitalization Medical Expenses and Post Hospitalization Medical expenses), Benefit 3 (Daily Allowance), Benefit 4 (Ambulance Cover), Benefit 5 (Organ Donor Cover), Benefit 7 (Automatic Recharge), Benefit 14 (Care Anywhere), Benefit 15 (Maternity cover), Optional Cover 3 (Unlimited Automatic Recharge), Optional Cover 7 (Smart Select), Optional Cover 10 (Additional Sum Insured for Accidental Hospitalization) and Optional Cover 14 (Air Ambulance Cover). The event giving rise to a Claim under Benefit 1 shall be within the Policy Period for the Claim of such Benefit to be accepted.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0084,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(c),"The maximum, total and cumulative liability of the Company in respect of an Insured Person for any and all Claims arising under this Policy during the Policy Year shall not exceed the Total Sum Insured for that Insured Person.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-EXC-0085,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(I),"On Floater Basis, the Company's maximum, total and cumulative liability, for any and all Claims incurred during the Policy Year in respect of all Insured Persons, shall not exceed the Total Sum Insured.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0086,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(II),"For any single Claim during a Policy Year, the maximum Claim amount payable shall be sum total of Base Sum Insured, No Claims Bonus (Benefit 10), No Claims Bonus Super (Optional Cover 4), Loyalty Bonus (Optional Cover19) and Additional Sum Insured for Accidental Hospitalization (Optional Cover 10). (NOTE: This clause is not applicable to Optional Cover 9: Personal Accident).",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0087,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(III),"All Claims shall be payable subject to the terms, conditions, exclusions, sub-limits and wait periods of the Policy and subject to availability of the Total Sum Insured.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0088,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(d),"Any Claim paid for Benefits namely Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses), Benefit 2 (Pre Hospitalization Medical Expenses and Post Hospitalization Medical Expenses), Benefit 3 (Daily Allowance), Benefit 4 (Ambulance Cover), Benefit 5 (Organ Donor Cover), Benefit 6 (Domiciliary Hospitalization), Benefit 9 (AYUSH Treatments), Benefit 11 (Global coverage (excluding U.S.A.), Benefit 13 (Vaccination Cover), Benefit 14 (Care Anywhere), Benefit 15 (Maternity cover), Benefit 17 (Global Plus) and Optional Covers namely Optional Cover 1 (Global Coverage – Total), Optional Cover 7 (Smart Select), Optional Cover 13 (Extension of Global Coverage), and Optional Cover 14 (Air Ambulance Cover), shall reduce the Total Sum Insured for the Policy Year and only the balance shall be available for all the future claims for that Policy Year.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0089,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(e),"Any Benefit or Optional cover specified to be payable under Cashless facility, would follow the procedures and settlement clauses mentioned as per Clause 6.1.2 (a).",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0090,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(f),"Any Benefit or Optional cover specified to be payable under Reimbursement facility, would follow the procedures and settlement clauses mentioned as per Clause 6.1.2 (b).",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0091,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(g),"The Co-payment, if and as specified in the Policy Schedule, shall be borne by the Policyholder / Insured Person on each Claim which will be applicable on Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses), Benefit 2 (Pre Hospitalization Medical Expenses and Post Hospitalization Medical Expenses), Benefit 4 (Ambulance Cover), Benefit 5 (Organ Donor Cover), Benefit 6 (Domiciliary Hospitalization), Benefit 9 (AYUSH Treatments), Benefit 11 (Global Coverage (excluding U.S.A.)), Benefit 14 (Care Anywhere), Benefit 13 (Vaccination Cover), Benefit 15 (Maternity cover), Benefit 17 (Global Plus), Optional Cover 1 (Global Coverage – Total), Optional Cover 10 (Additional Sum Insured for Accidental Hospitalization), Optional Cover 13 (Extension of Global Coverage) and Optional Cover 14 (Air Ambulance Cover).",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0092,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(h),"Deductible Option (if opted) is applicable on the Benefits namely Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses), Benefit 2 (Pre Hospitalization Medical Expenses and Post Hospitalization Medical Expenses), Benefit 4 (Ambulance Cover), Benefit 5 (Organ Donor Cover), Benefit 6 (Domiciliary Hospitalization), Benefit 9 (AYUSH Treatments), Benefit 11 (Global Coverage – excluding U.S.A.), Benefit 14 (Care Anywhere), Benefit 15 (Maternity cover), Benefit 17 (Global Plus), Optional Cover 1 (Global Coverage – Total), Optional Cover 10 (Additional Sum Insured for Accidental Hospitalization), Optional Cover 13 (Extension of Global Coverage) and Optional Cover 14 (Air Ambulance Cover).",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0093,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(k),"Coverage amount limits for Optional Cover 2 'Travel Plus', Optional Cover 6 'Everyday Care', Optional Cover 8 'OPD Care', Optional Cover 9 'Personal Accident' and Optional Cover 10 'Additional Sum Insured for Accidental Hospitalization' are covered over and above the Base Sum Insured (as defined under Definition 2.2.26).",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0094,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(l),"If Insured persons belonging to the same family are covered on an Individual basis, then every Insured person can opt for different Sum Insured and different Optional Covers.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0095,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(m),This Policy covers only medical treatment taken entirely within India unless otherwise specified under any Benefit or Optional Cover.,COVERAGE,True,This Policy covers only medical treatment taken entirely within India unless otherwise specified under any Benefit or Optional Cover.,
CARE-COV-0096,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3(n),Linear interpolation methodology will be applied to calculate the premium rates if an intermittent value of Sum Insured/sub-limit/benefit amount is chosen by the Policyholder.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0097,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1,Benefit 1: Hospitalization Expenses If an Insured Person is diagnosed with an Illness or suffers an Injury which requires the Insured Person to be admitted in a Hospital in India which should be Medically Necessary during the Policy Period and while the Policy is in force for:,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0098,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(i),"In-patient Care: The Company will indemnify the Policy Holder/Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred towards Hospitalization, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, maximum up to the Base Sum Insured as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Hospitalization is for a minimum period of 24 consecutive hours and was prescribed in written, by a Medical Practitioner, and the Medical Expenses incurred are Reasonable and Customary Charges that were Medically Necessary.",COVERAGE,True,"In-patient Care: The Company will indemnify the Policy Holder/Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred towards Hospitalization, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, maximum up to the Base Sum Insured as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Hospitalization is for a minimum period of 24 consecutive hours and was prescribed in written, by a Medical Practitioner, and the Medical Expenses incurred are Reasonable and Customary Charges that were Medically Necessary.",24 hours
CARE-COV-0099,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(ii),"Day Care Treatment: The Company will indemnify the Policy Holder/Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred on Day Care Treatment which involves a Surgical procedure, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, maximum up to the Base Sum Insured specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Day Care Treatment is listed as per the Annexure-I to Policy Terms & Conditions and period of treatment of the Insured Person in the Hospital/Day Care Centre does not exceed 24 hours, which would otherwise require an in-patient admission and such Day Care Treatment was prescribed in written, by a Medical Practitioner, and the Medical Expenses incurred are Reasonable and Customary Charges that were Medically Necessary.",COVERAGE,True,"Day Care Treatment: The Company will indemnify the Policy Holder/Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred on Day Care Treatment which involves a Surgical procedure, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, maximum up to the Base Sum Insured specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Day Care Treatment is listed as per the Annexure-I to Policy Terms & Conditions and period of treatment of the Insured Person in the Hospital/Day Care Centre does not exceed 24 hours, which would otherwise require an in-patient admission and such Day Care Treatment was prescribed in written, by a Me",24 hours
CARE-COV-0100,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(iii),Conditions applicable for Hospitalization Expenses (Benefit 1):,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0101,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,1,"If the Insured Person is admitted in a Hospital room where the Room Category opted or Room Rent incurred is higher than the eligible Room Category/ Room Rent as specified in the Policy Schedule, then,.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0102,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,1(II),"If specifically mentioned in the Policy Schedule that the Room Category/ Room Rent eligibility is “Single Private Room(upgradable to next level)”, it means such up-gradation will trigger only if Single Private Room is not available in the Hospital at the time of admission and Company's liability will arise only after accepting required documented proof for such Room unavailability. In case such documented proof is not furnished, then the maximum eligible Room Category would be considered as Single Private Room only.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0103,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2,"Single Private Room If the Policy Schedule states 'Single Private Room' as eligible Room Category, it means the maximum eligible Room Category in case of Hospitalization of the Insured Person payable by the Company is limited to stay in a Single Private Room.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0104,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3,"Single Private Room (upgradable to next level): If the Policy Schedule states 'Single Private Room (upgradable to next level)' as eligible Room Category, it means the maximum eligible Room Category in case of Hospitalization of the Insured Person payable by the Company is limited to stay in a Single Private Room or a Single Private Room of the immediate next category.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0105,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,4,"If the Policy Schedule states 'up to 1% of the Sum Insured per day' as eligible Room Rent, it means the maximum eligible Room Rent of the Insured Person payable by the Company is limited to 1% of the Sum Insured per day of Hospitalization. Any amount accrued as No Claims Bonus under (Benefit 10) or No Claims Bonus Super (Optional Cover 4) or Loyalty Bonus (Optional Cover 19), shall not form part of Base Sum Insured.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0106,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,5,"The nomenclature of Room categories may vary from one hospital to the other. Hence, the final consideration will be as per the definition of the Rooms mentioned in the Policy.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-EXC-0107,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,1,"If the Policy Schedule states 'up to 2% of the Sum Insured per day' as eligible ICU Charges per day of Hospitalization, it means the maximum eligible ICU charges of the Insured Person payable by the Company is limited to 2% of the Sum Insured per day of Hospitalization. Any amount accrued as No Claims Bonus (Benefit 10) or No Claims Bonus Super (Optional Cover 4) or Loyalty Bonus (Optional Cover 19) shall not form part of Base Sum Insured.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-DEF-0108,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2,"If the Policy Schedule states the eligibility of ICU Charges of the Insured Person as 'no sub-limit', it means that there is no separate restriction on ICU Charges incurred towards stay in ICU during Hospitalization.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0109,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2,"The Company will indemnify the Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred in respect of the below mentioned Ailments/ Procedures up to the amount specified against each and every Ailment/ Procedure mentioned in the Policy Schedule in a Policy Year, provided that the treatment was taken on the advice of a Medical Practitioner. (These conditions will apply only if specifically mentioned in the Policy Schedule)",COVERAGE,True,"The Company will indemnify the Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred in respect of the below mentioned Ailments/ Procedures up to the amount specified against each and every Ailment/ Procedure mentioned in the Policy Schedule in a Policy Year, provided that the treatment was taken on the advice of a Medical Practitioner.",
CARE-COV-0110,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2,Note: Sub-limits shall apply to total claim amount payable under all Hospitalization related benefits listed in base Plan (iv) Advance Technology Methods:,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0111,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2,The Company will indemnify the Insured Person up to Base Sum Insured for expenses incurred under Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses) for treatment taken through following advance technology methods:,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0112,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,2,L. Stem cell therapy: Hematopoietic stem cells for bone marrow transplant for haematological conditions to be covered.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0113,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.2,"Benefit 2: Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses and Post-hospitalization Medical Expenses The Company will indemnify the Policy Holder/Insured Person for Relevant Medical Expenses incurred which are Medically Necessary, only through Reimbursement Facility, maximum up to the Base Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Medical Expenses so incurred are related to the same Illness/Injury for which the Company has accepted the Insured Person's Claim under Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses) and subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit 2: Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses and Post-hospitalization Medical Expenses The Company will indemnify the Policy Holder/Insured Person for Relevant Medical Expenses incurred which are Medically Necessary, only through Reimbursement Facility, maximum up to the Base Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Medical Expenses so incurred are related to the same Illness/Injury for which the Company has accepted the Insured Person's Claim under Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses) and subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARE-EXC-0114,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.2(i),"Under Relevant Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses, for a period of 30 days immediately prior to the Insured Person's date of admission to the Hospital, provided that the Company shall not be liable to make payment for any Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses that were incurred before the Policy Start Date; and (ii) Under Relevant Post-hospitalization Medical Expenses, for a period of 60 days immediately after the Insured Person's date of discharge from the Hospital.",EXCLUSION,True,"Under Relevant Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses, for a period of 30 days immediately prior to the Insured Person's date of admission to the Hospital, provided that the Company shall not be liable to make payment for any Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses that were incurred before the Policy Start Date; and (ii) Under Relevant Post-hospitalization Medical Expenses, for a period of 60 days immediately after the Insured Person's date of discharge from the Hospital.",30 days; 60 days
CARE-COV-0115,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.3,"Benefit 3: Daily Allowance The Company will pay a fixed amount as specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, for each continuous and completed period of 24 hours of Hospitalization of the Insured Person, subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit 3: Daily Allowance The Company will pay a fixed amount as specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, for each continuous and completed period of 24 hours of Hospitalization of the Insured Person, subject to the conditions specified below:",24 hours
CARE-EXC-0116,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.3(i),The Company shall not be liable to make payment under this Benefit for more than 5 consecutive days of Hospitalization for each period of Hospitalization arising from Any One Illness or Accident; and (ii) This Benefit is valid for In-patient Care Hospitalization of the Insured Person only.,EXCLUSION,False,,5 days
CARE-COV-0117,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.4,"Benefit 4: Ambulance Cover The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the Base Sum Insured specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, for the Reasonable and Customary Charges necessarily incurred on availing road Ambulance services offered by a Hospital or by an Ambulance service provider for the Insured Person's necessary transportation through road, provided that the necessity of such Ambulance transportation is certified by the treating Medical Practitioner and subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit 4: Ambulance Cover The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the Base Sum Insured specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, for the Reasonable and Customary Charges necessarily incurred on availing road Ambulance services offered by a Hospital or by an Ambulance service provider for the Insured Person's necessary transportation through road, provided that the necessity of such Ambulance transportation is certified by the treating Medical Practitioner and subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARE-COV-0118,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.5,"Benefit 5: Organ Donor Cover The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the amount specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, for the Medical Expenses incurred in respect of the donor, for any organ transplant surgery during the Policy Year, subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit 5: Organ Donor Cover The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the amount specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, for the Medical Expenses incurred in respect of the donor, for any organ transplant surgery during the Policy Year, subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARE-COV-0119,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.5(i),"The Organ donor is an eligible donor in accordance with The Transplantation of Human Organs Act, 1994 (amended) and other applicable laws and rules.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0120,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.5(iii),The Company will not be liable to pay the Medical Expenses incurred by the Insured Person towards Pre-Hospitalization Medical Expenses and Post Hospitalization Medical Expenses (Benefit 2) or any other Medical Expenses in respect of the donor consequent to the harvesting.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0121,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.5(iv),"Clause 4.2 (10) under Permanent Exclusions, is superseded to the extent covered under this Benefit.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0122,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.6,"Benefit 6: Domiciliary Hospitalization The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, only through Reimbursement Facility, up to the amount specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, for the Medical Expenses incurred towards Domiciliary Hospitalization, i.e., Coverage extended when Medically Necessary treatment is taken at home (as explained in Definition 2.1.14), subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit 6: Domiciliary Hospitalization The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, only through Reimbursement Facility, up to the amount specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, for the Medical Expenses incurred towards Domiciliary Hospitalization, i.e., Coverage extended when Medically Necessary treatment is taken at home (as explained in Definition 2.1.14), subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARE-EXC-0123,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.6(iv),Any Pre Hospitalization Medical Expenses and Post Hospitalization Medical Expenses (Benefit 2) shall not be payable under this Benefit.,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-EXC-0124,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.6(v),Any Medical Expenses incurred for the treatment in relation to any of the following diseases shall not be payable under this Benefit:,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0125,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.7,"Benefit 7 : Automatic Recharge If a Claim is payable under the Policy, then the Company agrees to automatically make the re- instatement of up to the Base Sum Insured once in a policy year which is valid for that Policy Year only, subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit 7 : Automatic Recharge If a Claim is payable under the Policy, then the Company agrees to automatically make the re- instatement of up to the Base Sum Insured once in a policy year which is valid for that Policy Year only, subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARE-COV-0126,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.7(i),"The Recharge shall be utilized only after the base Sum Insured, No Claims Bonus (Benefit – 10), No Claims Bonus Super (Optional Cover – 4), Loyalty Bonus (Optional Cover 19) and Additional Sum Insured for Accidental Hospitalization (Optional Cover – 10) has been cumulatively exhausted in that Policy Year.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0127,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.7(ii),A Claim will be admissible under the Recharge only if the Claim is admissible under Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses) and Sum Insured applicable under clause 3.1.7.(i) is completely exhausted (iii) The Recharge is applicable only for Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses).,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0128,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.7(v),"No Claims Bonus (Benefit – 10), No Claims Bonus Super (Optional Cover – 4), Loyalty Bonus (Optional Cover 19) shall not be considered while calculating 'Automatic Recharge'.",EXCLUSION,False,,
