CARE-COV-0165,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.13,"The Company will indemnify the Insured Person up to the amount specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, towards Vaccination expenses for the Insured Person(s) up to 18 years of Age, as prescribed in the National Immunization Schedule (NIS) for protection against Diphtheria, Pertussis, Tetanus, Polio, Measles, Hepatitis B and Tuberculosis, which fall under category of Vaccine preventable diseases as per the Grid provided below.",COVERAGE,False,,18 years
CARE-COV-0166,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.14,"Benefit 14: Care Anywhere The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, for the Medical Expenses incurred towards the Insured Person's Major Illness / Injury treatment undertaken outside India, during the Policy Year, up to the Base Sum Insured specified in the Policy Schedule, subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit 14: Care Anywhere The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, for the Medical Expenses incurred towards the Insured Person's Major Illness / Injury treatment undertaken outside India, during the Policy Year, up to the Base Sum Insured specified in the Policy Schedule, subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARE-COV-0167,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.14(i),The Medical Expenses incurred towards the major Illness / injury treatment which are covered as a part of this Benefit are:,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0168,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,12,Total Blindness (ii) The Medical Expenses incurred are only for 'In-patient Care' or 'Day Care Treatment' undertaken in any Hospital; 'Pre-Hospitalization' and 'Post-Hospitalization' expenses is not covered under the purview of this cover.,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0169,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,12(iii),"The rate of exchange as published by Reserve Bank of India (RBI) or any other competent authority as on the Date of Loss shall be used for conversion of foreign currency amounts into Indian Rupees for payment of any Claim under this Benefit. Where on the Date of Loss, RBI rates are not published, the rates next published by RBI shall be considered for conversion.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0170,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,12(iv),The Company shall be liable to make payment under this Benefit only if prior written notice of at least 7 days is given to the Company.,COVERAGE,False,,7 days
CARE-COV-0171,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.15,"Benefit 15: Maternity Cover The Company shall indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, for the Medical Expenses associated with Hospitalization of an Insured Person for the delivery of a child, up to amount specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit 15: Maternity Cover The Company shall indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, for the Medical Expenses associated with Hospitalization of an Insured Person for the delivery of a child, up to amount specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARE-WAI-0172,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.15(a),Claims will not be admissible for any expenses incurred for diagnosis / treatment related to any Maternity Expenses until 24 months since the inception of the first Policy with the company.,WAITING_PERIOD,False,,24 months
CARE-COV-0173,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.15(b),This Benefit is available only under Floater cover type for all Insured Persons of age 18 years or above.,COVERAGE,False,,18 years
CARE-EXC-0174,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.15(c),Maternity Expenses incurred in connection with the voluntary medical termination of pregnancy during the first 12 weeks from the date of conception shall not be admissible under this Benefit.,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-EXC-0175,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.15(d),"Medical Expenses for ectopic pregnancy are not covered under this Benefit. However, these expenses are covered under Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses).",EXCLUSION,True,"However, these expenses are covered under Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses).",
CARE-EXC-0176,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.15(f),"Clause 4.1 (b) (15) under Permanent Exclusions, is superseded to the extent covered under this Benefit.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0177,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.16,"Wellness Benefit a. Insured Person who is covered as an Adult aged 18 years and above in the Policy can avail following, provided this benefit is opted for– Discount on renewal Premium by accumulating Healthy days as per table given below. One Healthy day can be accumulated by recording 10,000 steps (8000 steps for Insured Person of age 60 years and above) or more in single day through tracking apps, devices, etc.",COVERAGE,False,,18 years; 60 years
CARE-COV-0178,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.16,"120 10% Less than 120 0% - The above benefit will be applicable on Individual basis. In case of floater, average of number of Healthy days earned by all Insured Members shall be considered for calculating renewal discount. For example,' A' has attained 260 Healthy days and ' B' has attained 230 Healthy days, average of the Healthy days is 245 and accordingly the discount calculated is 20%.In case of multi tenure, average of number of Healthy days earned over the policy tenure shall be considered for discount.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0179,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.16,- The above section of benefit is available only for Insured covered as Adults aged 18 and above in the Policy and discount calculated shall be applicable on total premium of Policy.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0180,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.16,b. The company shall not be responsible for any disputes arising between the Insured Person and the empanelled Provider.,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0181,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.16,"c. The network under this benefit, does not constitute medical advice of any kind and it is not intended to be, and should not be, used to diagnose or identify treatment for a medical or mental health condition.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0182,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.17,"Global Plus The Company shall indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement facility, for Medically Necessary Inpatient Care and Day Care Treatment expenses incurred outside India up to the Sum Insured specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, during the Policy Year, subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Global Plus The Company shall indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement facility, for Medically Necessary Inpatient Care and Day Care Treatment expenses incurred outside India up to the Sum Insured specified against this Benefit in the Policy Schedule, during the Policy Year, subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARE-EXC-0183,Care Health,Care,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.17,- Proof of diagnosis within India - Insured's Passport and Visa (ii) The Medical expenses payable shall be limited to Inpatient Care & Day Care Treatment under Benefit 1 (Hospitalization Expenses) only; 'Pre-Hospitalization' and 'Post-Hospitalization' expenses are not covered under the purview of this cover.,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0184,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,,The Policy provides the following Optional Covers which can be opted either at the inception of the policy or at the time of renewal. The Policy Schedule will specify the Optional Covers that are in force for the Insured Persons.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0185,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.1,"Optional Cover 1: Global Coverage – Total “Global Coverage – Total” is an extension to Benefit 11 (Global Coverage (excluding U.S.A.)) and hence all the provisions stated under Clause 3.1.11, holds good for Clause 3.2.1 as well, except that the geographical scope of coverage through Optional Cover 1 is extended to United States of America also.",COVERAGE,True,"Optional Cover 1: Global Coverage – Total “Global Coverage – Total” is an extension to Benefit 11 (Global Coverage (excluding U.S.A.)) and hence all the provisions stated under Clause 3.1.11, holds good for Clause 3.2.1 as well, except that the geographical scope of coverage through Optional Cover 1 is extended to United States of America also.",
CARE-COV-0186,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2,"Optional Cover 2: Travel Plus The Benefits under this Optional Cover are valid outside India, which will be available for 45 continuous days from the date of travel in a Single Trip and 90 days on a cumulative basis as a whole, in a Policy Year.",COVERAGE,False,,45 days; 90 days
CARE-COV-0187,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2,"This Optional Cover includes six varied Benefits namely “Worldwide In-Patient Cover (for Emergency)”, “Worldwide OPD Cover”, “Loss of Passport”, “Loss of Checked-in Baggage”, “Repatriation of Mortal Remains” and “Medical Evacuation” which are explained below.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0188,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2,a. Worldwide In-Patient Cover (for Emergency),COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0189,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2,"If an Insured Person suffers an Injury or is diagnosed with an Illness as an Emergency condition that requires the Insured Person to take an In-patient Treatment which should be Medically Necessary, then the Insured Person can avail a 'Single Private Room' during the Hospitalization and the Company shall indemnify such relevant & reasonable Medical Expenses incurred by Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the Base Sum Insured as specified in the Policy Schedule or Rs. 20 Lakhs (whichever is lesser), subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"If an Insured Person suffers an Injury or is diagnosed with an Illness as an Emergency condition that requires the Insured Person to take an In-patient Treatment which should be Medically Necessary, then the Insured Person can avail a 'Single Private Room' during the Hospitalization and the Company shall indemnify such relevant & reasonable Medical Expenses incurred by Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the Base Sum Insured as specified in the Policy Schedule or Rs. 20 Lakhs (whichever is lesser), subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARE-EXC-0190,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2(i),"The In-patient Hospitalization is on the written advice of a Medical Practitioner, and the Medical Expenses incurred are Reasonable and Customary Charges that were Medically Necessary; 'Day Care Treatment', 'Pre-Hospitalization' and 'Post- Hospitalization' expenses are not covered under the purview of this cover.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0191,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2,"under this Benefit shall be reduced by the Deductible of Rs. 5,000. The Company shall be liable to make payment under the Policy for any Claim in respect of the Insured Person only when the Deductible on that Claim is exhausted.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0192,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2(i),"If an Insured Person while on a foreign land suffers an Injury or is diagnosed with an Illness, that requires the Insured Person to take an Out-patient Treatment, then the Company shall indemnify such Medical Expenses, through Reimbursement Facility, up to the Base Sum Insured as specified in the Policy Schedule or Rs. 20 Lakhs (whichever is lesser).",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0193,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2(ii),"The amount assessed by the Company on each admitted Claim for the Insured Person under this Benefit shall be reduced by the Deductible of Rs. 5,000. The Company shall be liable to make payment under the Policy for any Claim in respect of the Insured Person only when the Deductible on that Claim is exhausted.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0194,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2(i),"If an Insured Person loses his / her original passport, then the Company will indemnify the Insured Person up to 1% of the Base Sum Insured specified in the Policy Schedule or Rs. 20,000 (whichever is lesser), towards obtaining a duplicate or new passport.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0195,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2(ii),"The amount assessed by the Company on each admitted Claim for the Insured Person under this Benefit shall be reduced by the Deductible of Rs. 2,500. The Company shall be liable to make payment under the Policy for any Claim in respect of the Insured Person only when the Deductible on that Claim is exhausted.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0196,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2(iii),Additional Documents to be submitted for any Claim under this Benefit :,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-WAI-0197,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2,It is a condition precedent to the Company's liability under this Benefit that the following information and documentation shall be submitted to the Company or the Assistance Service Provider immediately and in any event within 30 days of the event giving rise to the Claim under this Benefit:,WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
CARE-COV-0198,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2,"d. Loss of Checked-in Baggage If the entire Checked-In Baggage is lost whilst in the custody of the Common Carrier, the Company will indemnify to the extent of cost incurred by the Insured Person towards replacement of the entire baggage and its contents as per market value, up to 1% of the Base Sum Insured specified in the Policy Schedule or Rs. 20,000 (whichever is lesser), subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Loss of Checked-in Baggage If the entire Checked-In Baggage is lost whilst in the custody of the Common Carrier, the Company will indemnify to the extent of cost incurred by the Insured Person towards replacement of the entire baggage and its contents as per market value, up to 1% of the Base Sum Insured specified in the Policy Schedule or Rs. 20,000 (whichever is lesser), subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARE-COV-0199,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2(i),Coverage under this Benefit shall commence only after the Checked-In Baggage is entrusted to the Common Carrier and a receipt obtained and coverage under this Benefit shall terminate automatically on the Common Carrier reaching the Place of Destination specified in the ticket of the Insured Person during the Policy Period;,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0200,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2(iii),"If the lost/undelivered Checked-In Baggage is subsequently traced and offered for delivery to the Insured Person, the Insured Person shall refund the amount paid by the Company under this Benefit in full irrespective of whether delivery of the baggage is taken or not;",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0201,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2,"offered for delivery to the Insured Person, the Insured Person shall refund the amount paid by the Company under this Benefit attributable to the portion of Checked-in Baggage traced in full irrespective of whether delivery of the baggage is taken;",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0202,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2(viii),Additional Exclusions applicable to any Claim under this Benefit:,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-EXC-0203,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.2,"Any Claim in respect of the Insured Person for, arising out of or directly or indirectly due to any of the following shall not be admissible under this Benefit unless expressly stated to the contrary elsewhere in the Policy terms and conditions:",EXCLUSION,True,"Any Claim in respect of the Insured Person for, arising out of or directly or indirectly due to any of the following shall not be admissible under this Benefit unless expressly stated to the contrary elsewhere in the Policy terms and conditions:",
CARE-DEF-0204,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,5,"Valuables (Valuables shall mean and include photographic, audio, video, painting, computer and any other electronic equipment, telecommunications and electrical equipment, telescopes, binoculars, antiques, watches, jewelry and gems, furs and articles made of precious stones and metals).",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0205,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,5,"e. Repatriation of Mortal Remains If death of the Insured Person happens solely and directly due to an Insurable event, the Company shall indemnify the Policyholder, through Reimbursement Facility, up to the Base Sum Insured as specified in the Policy Schedule or Rs. 20 Lakhs (whichever is lesser), for the costs of repatriation of the mortal remains of the Insured Person back to the Place of Residence or for a local burial or cremation at the place where death has occurred.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-WAI-0206,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,5,It is a condition precedent to the Company's liability under this Benefit that the following information and documents shall be submitted to the Company or the Assistance Service Provider immediately and in any event within 30 days of the event giving rise to the Claim under this Benefit:,WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
CARE-COV-0207,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,5,"f. Medical Evacuation The Company shall indemnify up to the Base Sum Insured as specified in the Policy Schedule or Rs. 20 Lakhs (whichever is lesser), for the reasonable cost incurred towards the medical evacuation of the Insured Person in an Emergency, through an Ambulance, including Air Ambulance or any other transportation and evacuation services to the nearest Hospital, (including necessary medical care en-route forming part of the treatment) for any Illness contracted or Injury sustained by the Insured Person during the Policy Year, subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Medical Evacuation The Company shall indemnify up to the Base Sum Insured as specified in the Policy Schedule or Rs. 20 Lakhs (whichever is lesser), for the reasonable cost incurred towards the medical evacuation of the Insured Person in an Emergency, through an Ambulance, including Air Ambulance or any other transportation and evacuation services to the nearest Hospital, (including necessary medical care en-route forming part of the treatment) for any Illness contracted or Injury sustained by the Insured Person during the Policy Year, subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARE-EXC-0208,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,5(ii),These transportation expenses are limited to transporting the Insured Person from the place of contracting or sustaining such Illness or Injury to the nearest appropriate Hospital. Any transportation from one hospital to another is not covered under this Benefit;,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0209,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,5(iii),"This benefit will be extended only through Cashless Facility, if the costs are certified and authorized by the Company or the Assistance Service Provider in advance, unless the Insured Person has a Life Threatening Medical Condition and the Insured Person (or his representatives) arrange for the emergency Medical evacuation at their own cost and expense in which case the Company will indemnify the costs incurred on the emergency Medical evacuation in accordance with the terms of this Benefit.;",COVERAGE,True,"This benefit will be extended only through Cashless Facility, if the costs are certified and authorized by the Company or the Assistance Service Provider in advance, unless the Insured Person has a Life Threatening Medical Condition and the Insured Person (or his representatives) arrange for the emergency Medical evacuation at their own cost and expense in which case the Company will indemnify the costs incurred on the emergency Medical evacuation in accordance with the terms of this Benefit.;",
CARE-COV-0210,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,5(iv),Payment under this Ben efit is subject to a Claim for the same Illness or Injury being admitted by the Company under Benefit 3.2.2.1 (Worldwide In-Patient Cover (for Emergency));,COVERAGE,True,Payment under this Ben efit is subject to a Claim for the same Illness or Injury being admitted by the Company under Benefit 3.2.2.1 (Worldwide In-Patient Cover (for Emergency));,
CARE-EXC-0211,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,5,"Any Claim in respect of any Insured Person for, arising out of or directly or indirectly due to any of the following shall not be admissible under this Optional cover unless expressly stated to the contrary elsewhere in the Policy terms and conditions:",EXCLUSION,True,"Any Claim in respect of any Insured Person for, arising out of or directly or indirectly due to any of the following shall not be admissible under this Optional cover unless expressly stated to the contrary elsewhere in the Policy terms and conditions:",
CARE-COV-0212,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,7,"Note for Deductible under 'Worldwide In-Patient Cover (for emergency)', 'Worldwide OPD Cover' and 'Loss of Passport' of Optional Cover 'Travel Plus' – Once the claimed amount is converted into Indian Rupees, the deductible (in INR) will be applied to calculate the final pay-out to the Claimant.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0213,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.3,"Optional Cover 3: Unlimited Automatic Recharge “Unlimited Automatic Recharge” is an extension to Benefit 7 (Automatic Recharge) and hence all the provisions stated under Clause 3.1.7, holds good for Clause 3.2.3 as well, except that the Recharge shall be available unlimited time during the Policy Year. However, in case of a single claim payout, the maximum liability of the Company shall not exceed the Base Sum Insured. No Claims Bonus (Benefit – 10), No Claims Bonus Super (Optional Cover – 4), Loyalty Bonus (Optional Cover 19) shall not be considered while calculating 'Unlimited Automatic Recharge'.",EXCLUSION,True,"Optional Cover 3: Unlimited Automatic Recharge “Unlimited Automatic Recharge” is an extension to Benefit 7 (Automatic Recharge) and hence all the provisions stated under Clause 3.1.7, holds good for Clause 3.2.3 as well, except that the Recharge shall be available unlimited time during the Policy Year.",
CARE-COV-0214,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.4,"Optional Cover 4: No Claims Bonus Super “No Claims Bonus Super” is an extension to Benefit 10 (No Claims Bonus) and hence all the provisions stated under Clause 3.1.10, holds good for Clause 3.2.4 as well, except the below clauses which have been modified for the purpose of this Optional Cover:",COVERAGE,True,"Optional Cover 4: No Claims Bonus Super “No Claims Bonus Super” is an extension to Benefit 10 (No Claims Bonus) and hence all the provisions stated under Clause 3.1.10, holds good for Clause 3.2.4 as well, except the below clauses which have been modified for the purpose of this Optional Cover:",
CARE-COV-0215,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.4(i),"If no Claim has been paid in the expiring Policy Year and the Policy is renewed with the Company without any break, the Insured Person would receive a flat 50% increase in the Base Sum Insured on a cumulative basis as a No Claims Bonus Super (which is over & above the Sum Insured accrued under Benefit 10 – No Claims Bonus), for each completed and continuous Policy Year.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0216,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.4(ii),"In any Policy Year, the accrued No Claims Bonus Super shall not exceed 100% of the total of the Sum Insured available in the renewed Policy.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0217,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.4(iv),"At the time of Policy renewal if the Policyholder chooses not to renew this Optional Cover, then the No Claims Bonus Super under the expiring Policy shall be forfeited.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0218,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.4(v),The Recharge amount ('Automatic Recharge' & 'Unlimited Automatic Recharge') shall not be considered while calculating 'No Claims Bonus Super'.,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0219,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.4(vi),"Along with the Benefits (Base Covers) under the Policy, accrued 'No Claims Bonus Super' can be utilized for Optional Cover 1 (Global Coverage – Total) and Optional Cover 13 (Extension of Global Coverage), if opted for.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0220,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.4,"If this Optional Cover is opted, then Policyholder is entitled for a discount on the Premium payable.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-EXC-0221,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.4,"3 500,000 100,000 250,000 400,000 400,000 150,000 350,000 Claim not payable.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARE-COV-0222,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.6,"Optional Cover 6: Everyday Care The Company will provide the following Everyday Care Services (the “Services”) to the Insured Person during the Policy Year, under this Optional Cover.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0223,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.6,"The Insured Person may avail out-patient treatment at any of the Company's Network Service Provider which is payable up to 1% of Base Sum Insured as specified in the Policy Schedule. For the purpose of this Benefit, a flat Co-payment of 20% per consultation is applicable and no other co-payment mentioned as per Clause 3 (g) or elsewhere in the Policy is applicable.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0224,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.6,"The Insured Person may avail Diagnostic Examination facilities anywhere within the Company's Network Service Provider which is payable up to 1% of Base Sum Insured as specified in the Policy Schedule, as prescribed by a Medical Practitioner. For the purpose of this Benefit, a flat Co-payment of 20% per Diagnostic Examination is applicable and no other co-payment mentioned as per Clause 3 (g) or elsewhere in the Policy is applicable.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0225,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.6,"Note: For the purpose of above Clause, Network Service Provider means any person, organization, institution that has been empanelled with the Company to provide Services specified under this Optional Cover to the Insured Person.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0226,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.7,"Optional Cover 7: Smart Select If this Optional Cover is opted, then Policyholder is entitled for a discount of 15% on the Premium payable, subject to following conditions:",COVERAGE,True,"Optional Cover 7: Smart Select If this Optional Cover is opted, then Policyholder is entitled for a discount of 15% on the Premium payable, subject to following conditions:",
CARE-COV-0227,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,2,"Payable as SI is exhausted (ii) However, no such additional co-payment shall be applicable if treatment is availed in the hospitals listed in Annexure IV to the Policy Terms and Conditions.",COVERAGE,True,"Payable as SI is exhausted (ii) However, no such additional co-payment shall be applicable if treatment is availed in the hospitals listed in Annexure IV to the Policy Terms and Conditions.",
CARE-COV-0228,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,2,This Benefit is available only within India and co-pay is not applicable for claims incurred outside India.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0229,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.8,"Optional Cover 8: OPD Care The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, only through Reimbursement Facility, for availing Out-Patient consultations, Diagnostic Examinations and Pharmacy expenses, up to the amount specified against this Optional Cover in the Policy Schedule, during the Policy Year, subject to the following condition:",COVERAGE,True,"Optional Cover 8: OPD Care The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, only through Reimbursement Facility, for availing Out-Patient consultations, Diagnostic Examinations and Pharmacy expenses, up to the amount specified against this Optional Cover in the Policy Schedule, during the Policy Year, subject to the following condition:",
CARE-COV-0230,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.8,- Coverage for Optional Cover 'OPD Care' is provided for entire Policy year and is available to all the Insured members in a Floater Policy type along with Individual Policy type.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0231,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.8,"- All the valid OPD claim expenses incurred by the Insured Person in a policy year will be payable / reimbursed by the Company. However, claim can be filed with the Company, only twice during that Policy year, as and when that Insured Person may deem fit.",COVERAGE,True,"However, claim can be filed with the Company, only twice during that Policy year, as and when that Insured Person may deem fit.",
CARE-COV-0232,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.9,"Optional Cover 9: Personal Accident The Insured Persons covered and the coverage amount chosen for the Proposer under this Optional Cover, are specified against this Optional Cover in the Policy Schedule.",COVERAGE,False,,
