CARE-COV-0234,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.9(i),"For Spouse: 50% of the coverage amount chosen for Proposer (ii) Per Child: 25% of the coverage amount chosen for Proposer (If opted for 'Per Child', cover should be taken for all dependent children under this Policy)",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0235,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.9,Proposer's Dependent parents are not eligible to for coverage under this Optional Cover 'Personal Accident'.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0236,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.9,"This Optional Cover includes two Benefits namely “Accidental Death” and “Permanent Total Disablement” which are explained below and are applicable to events arising worldwide:- a. Accidental Death If the Insured Person suffers an Injury during the Policy Period, which directly results in the Insured Person's death within 12 months from the date of Accident (including date of Accident), then the Company will pay 100% of the coverage amount of that Insured Person under this Optional Cover.",COVERAGE,False,,12 months
CARE-COV-0237,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.9,"Sr. No. Insured Events this Optional Cover i Total and irrecoverable loss of sight of both eyes, or of the actual loss by physical separation of two entire hands or two entire feet, or one entire hand and one entire foot, or the total and irrecoverable loss of sight of one eye and loss by physical separation of one entire hand or one entire foot ii Total and irrecoverable loss of (a) use of two hands or two feet; or (b) one hand and one foot; or (c) sight of one eye and use of one hand or one foot Amount payable = % of the coverage amount of that Insured Person under 100% 100% iii Total and irrecoverable loss of sight of one eye, or of the actual loss by physical separation of one entire hand or one entire foot 50% iv Total and irrecoverable loss of use of a hand or a foot without physical separation 50% v Paraplegia or Quadriplegia or Hemiplegia 100%.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-DEF-0238,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.9,"Note: For the purpose of Sr. No. I to IV above, physical separation of a hand or foot shall mean separation of the hand at or above the wrist, and of the foot at or above the ankle.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARE-COV-0239,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.9(i),"“Hemiplegia” means complete and irrecoverable paralysis of the arm, leg, and trunk on the same side of the body;",COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0240,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.9(ii),“Paraplegia” means complete and irrecoverable paralysis of the whole of the lower half of the body (below waist) including both the legs;,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0241,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.9(iii),“Quadriplegia” means complete and irrecoverable paralysis of all four limbs.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARE-COV-0242,Care Health,Care,3.2. OPTIONAL COVERS,3.2.9,Insured Event means an event that is covered under the Policy and which is in accordance with the Policy Terms & Conditions.,COVERAGE,False,,
