CARESU-COV-0372,Care Health,Care Supreme,General,,"In consideration of the premium paid by the Policy Holder, subject to the terms & conditions contained herein, the Company agrees to pay/indemnify the Insured Person(s), the amount of such expenses that are reasonably and necessarily incurred up to the limits specified against respective Benefit in any Policy Year.",COVERAGE,True,"In consideration of the premium paid by the Policy Holder, subject to the terms & conditions contained herein, the Company agrees to pay/indemnify the Insured Person(s), the amount of such expenses that are reasonably and necessarily incurred up to the limits specified against respective Benefit in any Policy Year.",
CARESU-WAI-0373,Care Health,Care Supreme,General,,"Please check whether the details given by you about the insured Persons in the proposal form (a copy of which was provided at the time of issuance of cover for the first time) are incorporated correctly in the policy schedule. If you find any discrepancy, please inform us within 30 days from the date of receipt of the policy, failing which the details relating to the person/s covered would be taken as correct.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
CARESU-WAI-0374,Care Health,Care Supreme,General,,"So also the coverage details may also be gone through and in the absence of any communication from you within 30 days from the date of receipt of the policy, it would be construed that the policy issued is correct and the claims if any arise under the policy will be dealt with based on proposal /policy details.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
CARESU-EXC-0375,Care Health,Care Supreme,General,,"For the purposes of interpretation and understanding of the product the Company has defined, herein below some of the important words used in the product and for the remaining language and the words the Company believes to mean the normal meaning of the English language as explained in the standard language dictionaries. The words and expressions defined in the Insurance Act, IRDA Act, regulations notified by the Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India (’Authority’) and circulars and guidelines issued by the Authority shall carry the meanings described therein. The terms and conditions, insurance coverage and exclusions, other Benefits, various procedures and conditions which have been built-in to the product are to be construed in accordance with the applicable provisions contained in the product.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0376,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.1,"Accidental/ Accident is a sudden, unforeseen and involuntary event caused by external, visible and violent means.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0377,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.3,"AYUSH Day Care Centre means and includes Community Health Centre (CHC), Primary Health Centre (PHC), Dispensary, Clinic, Polyclinic or any such center which is registered with the local authorities, wherever applicable, and having facilities for carrying out treatment procedures and medical or surgical/para-surgical interventions or both under the supervision of registered AYUSH Medical Practitioner (s) on daycare basis without in-patient services and must comply with all the following criterion:",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0378,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.4,"Cashless Facility means a facility extended by the insurer to the Insured where the payments, of the costs of treatment undergone by the insured in accordance with the Policy terms and conditions, are directly made to the network Provider by the insurer to the extent pre-authorization is approved.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0379,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.5,Condition Precedent shall mean a Policy term or condition upon which the Insurer's liability under the Policy is conditional upon.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0380,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.6,"Congenital Anomaly refers to a condition which is present since birth, and which is abnormal with reference to form, structure or position :",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0381,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.9,"Day Care Centre means any institution established for day care treatment . of illness and/or injuries or a medical setup within a hospital and which has been registered with the local authorities, wherever applicable, and is under the supervision of a registered and qualified medical practitioner AND must comply with all minimum criteria as under- a. has qualified nursing staff under its employment;",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0382,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.10,"Day Care Treatment means medical treatment, and/or Surgical Procedure which is:",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0383,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.10,Treatment normally taken on an out-patient basis is not included in the scope of this definition.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0384,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.11,Deductible is a cost-sharing requirement under a health insurance policy that provides that the Insurer will not be liable for a specified rupee amount in case of indemnity policies and for a specified number of days/hours in case of hospital cash policies which will apply before any benefits are payable by the insurer. A deductible does not reduce the Sum Insured.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0385,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.12,"Dental Treatment means a treatment related to teeth or structures supporting teeth including examinations, fillings (where appropriate), crowns, extractions and surgery.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0386,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.14,Domiciliary Hospitalization means medical treatment for an illness/disease/injury which in the normal course would require care and treatment at a Hospital but is actually taken while confined at home under any of the following circumstances:,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0387,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.15,"Emergency Care (Emergency) means management for an illness or injury which results in symptoms which occur suddenly and unexpectedly, and requires immediate care by a medical practitioner to prevent death or serious long term impairment of the insured Person's health.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-WAI-0388,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.16,"Grace Period means the specified period of time, immediately following the premium due date during which premium payment can be made to renew or continue a policy in force without loss of continuity benefits pertaining to waiting periods and coverage of pre-existing diseases. Coverage need not be available during the period for which no premium is received. The grace period for payment of the premium for all types of insurance policies shall be: fifteen days where premium payment mode is monthly and thirty days in all other cases.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
CARESU-COV-0389,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.16,"Provided the insurers shall offer coverage during the grace period, if the premium is paid in installments during the policy period.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0390,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.17,"Hospital (not applicable for Overseas Travel Insurance) means any institution established for in-patient care and day care treatment of illness and/or injuries and which has been registered as a hospital with the local authorities under the Clinical Establishments (Registration and Regulation) Act, 2010 or under the enactments specified under the Schedule of Section 56(1) of the said Act OR complies with all minimum criteria as under:",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0391,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.18,"Hospitalization (not applicable for Overseas Travel Insurance) means admission in a Hospital for a minimum period of 24 consecutive 'In-patient Care' hours except for specified procedures/treatments, where such admission could be for a period of less than 24 consecutive hours.",DEFINITION,True,"Hospitalization (not applicable for Overseas Travel Insurance) means admission in a Hospital for a minimum period of 24 consecutive 'In-patient Care' hours except for specified procedures/treatments, where such admission could be for a period of less than 24 consecutive hours.",24 hours
CARESU-DEF-0392,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.19,Illness means a sickness or a disease or a pathological condition leading to the impairment of normal physiological function and requires medical treatment.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0393,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.19(a),"Acute condition - Acute condition is a disease, illness or injury that is likely to respond quickly to treatment which aims to return the person to his or her state of health immediately before suffering the disease/ illness/ injury which leads to full recovery.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0394,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.19(b),"Chronic condition - A chronic condition is defined as a disease, illness, or injury that has one or more of the following characteristics:",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0395,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.20,"Injury means accidental physical bodily harm excluding illness or disease solely and directly caused by external, violent and visible and evident means which is verified and certified by a Medicl Practitioner.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0396,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.21,In-patient Care (not applicable for Overseas Travel Insurance) means treatment for which the Insured Person has to stay in a Hospital for more | than 24 hours for a covered event.,COVERAGE,False,,24 hours
CARESU-DEF-0397,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.22,"Intensive Care Unit (ICU) means an identified section, ward or wing of a Hospital which is under the constant supervision of a dedicated Medical Practitioner(s), and which is specially equipped for the continuous monitoring and treatment of patients who are in a critical condition, or require life support facilities and where the level of care and supervision is considerably more sophisticated and intensive than in the ordinary and other wards.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0398,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.23,"ICU Charges (Intensive care Unit) (Intensive care Unit) means the amount charged by a Hospital towards ICU expenses which shall include the expenses for ICU bed, general medical support services provided to any ICU patient including monitoring devices, critical care nursing and intensivist charges.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0399,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.25,Medical Advice means any consultation or advice from a Medical Practitioner including the issuance of any prescription or follow-up prescription.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0400,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.26,"Medical Expenses means those expenses that an Insured Person has necessarily and actually incurred for medical treatment on account of Illness or Accident on the advice of a Medical Practitioner, as long as these are no more than would have been payable if the Insured Person had not been insured and no more than other Hospitals or doctors in the same locality would have charged for the same medical treatment.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0401,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.28,"Medically Necessary Treatment (not applicable for Overseas Travel | Insurance) means any treatment, tests, medication, or stay in Hospital or part of a stay in Hospital which:",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-WAI-0402,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.29,"Migration means a facility provided to policyholders (including all members under family cover and group policies), to transfer the credits gained for pre-existing diseases and specific waiting periods from one health insurance policy to another with the same insurer.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0403,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.31,Newborn baby means baby born during the Policy Period and is aged up to 90 days.,DEFINITION,False,,90 days
CARESU-DEF-0404,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.32,"Non - Network Provider: Non-Network means any hospital, day care centre or other provider that is not part of the Company's network.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0405,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.33,Notification of Claim means the process of intimating a Claim to the Insurer or TPA through any of the recognized modes of communication.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-WAI-0406,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.35,"Portability means a facility provided to the health insurance policyholders (including all members under family cover), to transfer the credits gained for, pre-existing diseases and specific waiting periods from one insurer to another insurer.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
CARESU-WAI-0407,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.36,"Pre-existing Disease means any condition, ailment, injury or disease.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
CARESU-WAI-0408,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.36(i),That is/are diagnosed by a physician not more than 36 months prior to the date of commencement of the policy issued by the insurer; or.,WAITING_PERIOD,False,,36 months
CARESU-WAI-0409,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.36(ii),"For which medical advice or treatment was recommended by, or received from, a physician, not more than 36 months prior to the date of commencement of the policy.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,36 months
CARESU-DEF-0410,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.37,"Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses means Medical Expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days preceding the hospitalization of the Insured Person, provided that :",DEFINITION,True,"Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses means Medical Expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days preceding the hospitalization of the Insured Person, provided that :",
CARESU-DEF-0411,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.38,Post-hospitalization Medical Expenses means Medical Expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days immediately after the Insured Person is discharged from the Hospital provided that:,DEFINITION,True,Post-hospitalization Medical Expenses means Medical Expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days immediately after the Insured Person is discharged from the Hospital provided that:,
CARESU-DEF-0412,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.40,"Reasonable and Customary Charges (not applicable for Overseas Travel Insurance) means the charges for services or supplies, which are the standard charges for the specific provider and consistent with the prevailing charges in the geographical area for identical or similar services, taking into account the nature of the Illness/ Injury involved.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0413,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.41,"Renewal means the terms on which the contract of insurance can be renewed on mutual consent with a provision of grace period for treating the renewal continuous for the purpose of gaining credit for pre-existing diseases, time-bound exclusions and for all waiting periods.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0414,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.42,Room Rent Room Rent means the amount charged by a Hospital towards Room & Boarding expenses and shall include the associated medical expenses.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0415,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.43,Subrogation (Applicable to other than Health Policies and health sections of Travel and PA policies) means the right of the Insurer to assume the rights of the Insured Person to recover expenses paid out under the Policy that may be recovered from any other source.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0416,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.44,"Surgery/Surgical Procedure: means manual and/ or operative procedure(s) required for treatment of an Illness or Injury, correction of deformities and defects, diagnosis and cure of diseases, relief from suffering or prolongation of life, performed in a Hospital or a Day Care Centre by a Medical Practitioner.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0417,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.45,"Unproven/Experimental Treatment means a treatment including drug experimental therapy which is not based on established medical practice in India, is treatment experimental or unproven.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0418,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.46,"AYUSH treatment refers to the medical and/ or hospitalization treatments given under Ayurveda, Yoga and Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha and Homeopathy systems.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0419,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.47,"Break in policy means the period of gap that occurs at the end of the existing policy term/installment premium due date, when the premium due for renewal on a given policy or installment premium due is not paid on or before the premium renewal date or grace period.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0420,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.1. Standard Definitions,2.1.48,"Specific waiting period (Named Ailment Waiting Period) means a period up to 36 months from the commencement of a health insurance policy during which period specified diseases/treatments (except due to an accident) are not covered. On completion of the period, diseases/treatments shall be covered provided the policy has been continuously renewed without any break.",EXCLUSION,True,Specific waiting period (Named Ailment Waiting Period) means a period up to 36 months from the commencement of a health insurance policy during which period specified diseases/treatments (except due to an accident) are not covered.,36 months
CARESU-DEF-0421,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.1,Age means the completed age of the Insured Person as on his/her last birthday.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0422,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.2,Associate Medical Expenses means those Medical Expenses as listed below which vary in accordance with the Room Rent or room Category applicable in a Hospital:,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0423,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,1,The following expenses shall not be part of 'associate medical expenses':,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0424,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.3,Ambulance means a vehicle (Road/Air) operated by a licensed/ authorized service provider and equipped for the transport and paramedical treatment of persons requiring medical attention.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0425,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.4,Annexure means the document attached and marked as Annexure to this Policy.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0426,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.5,Claim means a demand made in accordance with the terms and conditions of the Policy for payment of the specified Benefits in respect of the Insured Person.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0427,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.6,Claimant means a person who possesses a relevant and valid Insurance Policy which is issued by the Company and is eligible to file a Claim in the event of a covered loss.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0428,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.7,Company (also referred as Insurer/We/Us) means Care Health Insurance Limited.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0429,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.8,"Diagnosis means pathological conclusion drawn by a registered medical practitioner, supported by acceptable Clinical, radiological, histological, histo-pathological and laboratory evidence wherever applicable.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0430,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.9,Excluded Providers means hospital or any other provider specifically excluded by the Insurer.,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0431,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.10,"Hazardous Activities (or Adventure sports) means any sport or activity, which is potentially dangerous to the Insured whether he is trained or not. Such sport/activity includes (but not limited to) stunt activities of any kind, adventure racing, base jumping, biathlon, big game hunting, black water rafting, BMX stunt/ obstacle riding, bobsleighing/ using skeletons, bouldering, boxing, canyoning, caving/ pot holing, cave tubing, rock climbing/ trekking/ mountaineering, cycle racing, cyclo cross, drag racing, endurance testing, hand gliding, harness racing, hell skiing, high diving (above 5 meters), hunting, ice hockey, ice speedway, jousting, judo, karate, kendo, lugging, risky manual labor, marathon running, martial arts, micro-lighting, modern pentathlon, motor cycle racing, motor rallying, parachuting, paragliding/ parapenting, piloting aircraft, polo, power lifting, power boat racing, quad biking, river boarding, scuba diving, river bugging, rodeo, roller hockey, rugby, ski acrobatics, ski doo, ski jumping, ski racing, sky diving, small bore target shooting, speed trials/ time trials, triathlon, water ski jumping, weight lifting or wrestling of any type.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0432,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.11,"Indemnity/Indemnify means compensating the Insured Person up to the extent of Expenses incurred, on occurrence of an event which results in a financial loss and is covered as the subject matter of the Insurance Cover.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0433,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.12,Insured Event means an event that is covered under the Policy; and which is in accordance with the Policy Terms & Conditions.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0434,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.13,"Insured Person (Insured) means a self, legally married spouse, dependent children, dependent parents or any other relationship having an insurable interest and whose name specifically appears under Insured in the Policy Schedule and with respect to whom the premium has been received by the Company.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0435,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.14,"Mental Illness means a substantial disorder of thinking, mood, perception, orientation or memory that grossly impairs judgment, behavior, capacity to recognize, reality or ability to meet the ordinary demands of life, mental conditions associated with the abuse of alcohol and drugs, but does not include mental retardation which is a condition of arrested or incomplete development of mind of a person, specially characterized by sub normality of intelligence.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0436,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.15,"Medical device means any, instrument, apparatus or device including any component, part or accessory thereof, manufactured solely for medical purpose which intends to treatment and mitigation of a medical condition or to physically support the function of human body.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0437,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.16,"Nominee means the person named in the Policy Schedule or as declared with the Policyholder who is nominated to receive the benefits under this Policy in accordance with the terms of the Policy, if the Insured Person is deceased.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0438,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.17,Preventive Care means any kind of treatment taken as a pro-active care measure without actual requirement or symptoms of a disease or illness.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0439,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.18,"Policy means these Policy terms and conditions and Annexures thereto, the Proposal Form, Policy Schedule and Optional Cover (if applicable) which form part of the Policy and shall be read together.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0440,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.20,Policy Year means a period of one year commencing on the Policy Period Start Date or any anniversary thereof.,DEFINITION,False,,1 year
CARESU-DEF-0441,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.21,Policyholder (also referred as You) means the person named in the Policy Schedule as the Policyholder.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0442,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.22,Policy Period means the period commencing from the Policy Period Start Date and ending on the Policy Period End Date of the Policy as specifically appearing in the Policy Schedule.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0443,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.24,"Policy Period Start Date means the date on which the Policy commences, as specifically appearing in the Policy Schedule.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0444,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.25,"Rehabilitation means assisting an Insured Person who, following a Medical Condition, requires assistance in physical, vocational, independent living and educational pursuits to restore him to the position in which he was in, prior to such medical condition occurring.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0445,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.26,"Sum Insured means the amount specified in the Policy Schedule, for which premium is paid by the Policyholder.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0446,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.27,Single Private AC Room means an air conditioned room in a Hospital where a single patient along with the attendant is accommodated and which has an attached toilet (lavatory and bath). Such room type shall be the most basic and the most economical of all accommodations available as a Single room in that Hospital.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0447,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.28,"Third Party Administrator or TPA means a Company registered with the Authority, and engaged by an insurer, for a fee or by whatever name called and as may be mentioned in the health services agreement, for providing health services as mentioned under IRDAI (TPA-Health Services) Regulations as amended from time to time.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0448,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.29,"Therapy - A therapy is the attempted remediation of a health problem, usually following a medical diagnosis. It means treatment to help or cure a mental or physical illness, usually without drugs or medical operations. This does not include any experimental therapies.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0449,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,2.2.30,Twin Sharing Room means a Hospital room where at least two patients are accommodated at the same time. Such room shall be the most basic and the most economical of all accommodations available as twin sharing rooms in that Hospital.,DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0450,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3,General Conditions Applicable To All The Benefits And Optional Benefits.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0451,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,1,"Child would be migrated to separate Policy of Company and treated as adult upon attaining age of 25 years or above at the time of renewal , unless eligible as Adult to be covered under this Policy.",COVERAGE,True,"Child would be migrated to separate Policy of Company and treated as adult upon attaining age of 25 years or above at the time of renewal , unless eligible as Adult to be covered under this Policy.",25 years
CARESU-EXC-0452,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,1,Insured Person for any and all Claims arising under this Policy during the Policy Year shall not exceed the Sum Insured as mentioned in the policy schedule against that benefit for that Insured Person.,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0453,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,1(I),"On Floater Basis, the Company's maximum, total and cumulative liability, for any and all Claims incurred during the Policy Year in respect of all Insured Persons, shall not exceed the Sum Insured as mentioned in the policy schedule.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0454,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,1(II),"For any single Claim including continuous Hospitalisation during a Policy Year, the maximum Claim amount payable shall be sum total of Sum Insured, Cumulative Bonus, Cumulative Bonus Super (if applicable), Plus Benefit (if applicable), Unlimited Care (if applicable).",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0455,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,1(III),"All Claims shall be payable subject to the terms, conditions, exclusions, sub-limits and wait periods of the Policy and subject to availability of the Sum Insured.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0456,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3,"Deductible Option (if opted) is applicable on the Benefits namely under Hospitalization Expenses, Road Ambulance Cover, Claim Shield , Plus Benefit, Air Ambulance Cover, Unlimited Care.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0457,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,4,"The Co-payment proportion ( If opted ) shall be borne by the Insured Person on each Claim which will be applicable on Benefits namely Hospitalization Expenses, Road Ambulance Cover , Optional Benefits- Claim Shield , Plus Benefit, Air Ambulance Cover, Unlimited Care.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0458,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,5,"Any Claim paid for Benefits namely Hospitalization Expenses (i.e. In-Patient Care, Day Care Treatment, Advance Technology Methods, Pre- Hospitalization Medical Expenses , Post-Hospitalization Medical Expenses , Organ Donor, Ayush Treatment and Domiciliary Hospitalization ) , Road Ambulance Cover , Claim Shield , Air Ambulance Cover shall reduce the Sum Insured for the Policy Year and only the balance shall be available for all the future claims for that Policy Year.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0459,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,6,"Admissibility of a Claim under Benefit “In-patient Care and/or Day Care Treatment” is a pre-condition to the admission of a Claim under Pre Hospitalization Medical Expenses and Post Hospitalization Medical expenses, Organ Donor Cover, Road Ambulance Cover, Claim Shield , Plus Benefit, Air Ambulance Cover and Unlimited Care and the event giving rise to a Claim under Benefit “In-patient Care and/or Day Care Treatment” shall be within the Policy Period for the Claim of such Benefit to be accepted.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0460,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,8,"If Insured Persons are covered on an Individual basis, then every Insured Person can opt for different Sum Insured and different Optional Benefits. If Insured Persons are covered on Floater basis, then the Optional benefits if opted shall available to all Insured Persons under floater policy unless specifically mentioned/catered to in the Policy.",COVERAGE,True,"If Insured Persons are covered on Floater basis, then the Optional benefits if opted shall available to all Insured Persons under floater policy unless specifically mentioned/catered to in the Policy.",
CARESU-COV-0461,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,9,Linear interpolation methodology will be applied to calculate the premium rates if an intermittent value of Sum Insured/sub-limit/benefit amount is chosen by the Policyholder.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0462,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,10,"The Company acts as facilitator for the services offered and shall not assume nor be deemed to assume, any liability for the quality, deficiencies or availability of services provided by the empaneled service providers.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0463,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1,Benefit : Hospitalization Expenses If an Insured Person is diagnosed with an illness or suffers an injury and which requires the Insured Person to be admitted in a Hospital in India which should be Medically Necessary during the Policy Year and while the Policy is in force for:,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0464,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(i),"Benefit: In-patient Care: The Company will indemnify the Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred towards Hospitalization through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, maximum up to the Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Hospitalization is for a minimum period of 24 consecutive hours and was prescribed in writing, by a Medical Practitioner, and the Medical Expenses incurred are Reasonable and Customary Charges that were Medically Necessary.",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit: In-patient Care: The Company will indemnify the Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred towards Hospitalization through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, maximum up to the Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Hospitalization is for a minimum period of 24 consecutive hours and was prescribed in writing, by a Medical Practitioner, and the Medical Expenses incurred are Reasonable and Customary Charges that were Medically Necessary.",24 hours
CARESU-COV-0465,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(ii),"Benefit: Day Care Treatment: The Company will indemnify the Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred on all Day Care Treatments through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, maximum up to the Sum Insured ,as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the period of treatment of the Insured Person in the Hospital/Day Care Centre does not exceed 24 hours, which would otherwise require an in-patient admission and such Day Care Treatments was prescribed in written, by a Medical Practitioner, and the Medical Expenses incurred are Reasonable and Customary Charges that were Medically Necessary.",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit: Day Care Treatment: The Company will indemnify the Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred on all Day Care Treatments through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, maximum up to the Sum Insured ,as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the period of treatment of the Insured Person in the Hospital/Day Care Centre does not exceed 24 hours, which would otherwise require an in-patient admission and such Day Care Treatments was prescribed in written, by a Medical Practitioner, and the Medical Expenses incurred are Reasonable and Customary Charges that were Medically Necessary.",24 hours
CARESU-COV-0466,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1,"Insured Person up to the Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, for expenses incurred under Benefit 'Hospitalization expenses ' for treatment taken through following advance technology methods:",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0467,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1,L. Stem cell therapy: Hematopoietic stem cells for bone marrow transplant for haematological conditions to be covered.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0468,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(iv),"Pre-Hospitalization Medical Expenses The Company will indemnify the Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred which are Medically Necessary, only through Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Medical Expenses so incurred are related to the same Illness/Injury for which the Company has accepted the Insured Person's Claim under Benefit 'Hospitalization Expenses' and subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Pre-Hospitalization Medical Expenses The Company will indemnify the Insured Person for Medical Expenses incurred which are Medically Necessary, only through Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Medical Expenses so incurred are related to the same Illness/Injury for which the Company has accepted the Insured Person's Claim under Benefit 'Hospitalization Expenses' and subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARESU-EXC-0469,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(i),"For a period of 60 days immediately prior to the Insured Person's date of admission to the Hospital, provided that the Company shall not be liable to make payment for any Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses that were not incurred during the Policy Year.",EXCLUSION,True,"For a period of 60 days immediately prior to the Insured Person's date of admission to the Hospital, provided that the Company shall not be liable to make payment for any Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses that were not incurred during the Policy Year.",60 days
CARESU-COV-0470,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(v),"Post-Hospitalization Medical Expenses Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Medical Expenses so incurred are related to the same Illness/Injury for which the Company has accepted the Insured Person's Claim under Benefit 'Hospitalization Expenses' and subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Post-Hospitalization Medical Expenses Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, provided that the Medical Expenses so incurred are related to the same Illness/Injury for which the Company has accepted the Insured Person's Claim under Benefit 'Hospitalization Expenses' and subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARESU-WAI-0471,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(i),For a period of 180 days immediately after the Insured Person's date of discharge from the hospital and claim documents to be submitted within 30 days after the completion of 180 days from the date of discharge from the hospital.,WAITING_PERIOD,False,,180 days; 30 days
CARESU-COV-0472,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(vi),"Benefit : AYUSH Treatment The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, towards Medical Expenses incurred with respect to the Insured Person's medical treatment undergone at any AYUSH Hospitals or health care facilities for any of the listed AYUSH Treatments namely Ayurveda, Yoga, Naturopathy, Sidha , Unani and Homeopathy, subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit : AYUSH Treatment The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, towards Medical Expenses incurred with respect to the Insured Person's medical treatment undergone at any AYUSH Hospitals or health care facilities for any of the listed AYUSH Treatments namely Ayurveda, Yoga, Naturopathy, Sidha , Unani and Homeopathy, subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARESU-COV-0473,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(i),A Claim will be admissible under this Benefit only if the Claim is admissible under Benefit 'Hospitalization Expenses'.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0474,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(ii),"Medical Treatment should be rendered from a registered Medical Practitioner who holds a valid practicing license in respect of such AYUSH Treatments; and (iii) Such treatment taken is within the jurisdiction of India; and (iv) Clause 4.2 (12) under Permanent Exclusions, is superseded to the extent covered under this Benefit.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0475,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(vii),"Benefit : Domiciliary Hospitalization The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, only through Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured ,as specified in the Policy Schedule, for the Medical Expenses incurred towards Domiciliary Hospitalization, i.e., Coverage extended when Medically Necessary treatment is taken at home (as explained in Definition 2.1.14), subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit : Domiciliary Hospitalization The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, only through Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured ,as specified in the Policy Schedule, for the Medical Expenses incurred towards Domiciliary Hospitalization, i.e., Coverage extended when Medically Necessary treatment is taken at home (as explained in Definition 2.1.14), subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARESU-COV-0476,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(iv),Any Pre Hospitalization Medical Expenses and Post Hospitalization Medical Expenses shall be payable under this Benefit.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0477,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.1(v),Any Medical Expenses incurred for the treatment in relation to any of the following diseases shall not be payable under this Benefit :,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0478,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,12(viii),"Benefit : Organ Donor Cover The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, for the Medical Expenses incurred in respect of the donor, for any organ transplant surgery during the Policy Year, subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit : Organ Donor Cover The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured, as specified in the Policy Schedule, for the Medical Expenses incurred in respect of the donor, for any organ transplant surgery during the Policy Year, subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARESU-COV-0479,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,12(i),"The Organ donor is an eligible donor in accordance with The Transplantation of Human Organs Act, 1994 (amended) and other applicable laws and rules.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0480,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,12(iii),The Company will not be liable to pay the Medical Expenses incurred by the Insured Person towards benefit 'Pre-Hospitalization Medical Expenses and Post Hospitalization M Medical Expenses' or any other Medical Expenses in respect of the donor consequent to the harvesting.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0481,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,12(ix),"Conditions applicable for Benefit ‘Hospitalization Expenses’ Room, boarding and nursing expenses as charged by the Hospital where the Insured Person availed medical treatment (Room Rent / Room Category):",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0482,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,12(i),"The eligible Room Rent or Room Category applicable for the Insured Person under the Policy is 'No limit', which means that there is no separate restriction on Room Charges incurred towards stay during Hospitalization.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0483,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,12(ii),"Intensive Care Unit Charges (ICU Charges): The eligible ICU Charges applicable for the Insured Person under the Policy is 'No limit', which means that there is no separate restriction on ICU Charges incurred towards stay in ICU during Hospitalization.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0484,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.2,"Benefit : Road Ambulance Cover The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured, provided that the Medical Expenses so incurred are related to the Illness or Injury for which the Company has accepted the Insured Person's Claim under Benefit 'Hospitalization Expenses' and subject to conditions as specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit : Road Ambulance Cover The Company will indemnify the Insured Person, through Cashless or Reimbursement Facility, up to the Sum Insured, provided that the Medical Expenses so incurred are related to the Illness or Injury for which the Company has accepted the Insured Person's Claim under Benefit 'Hospitalization Expenses' and subject to conditions as specified below:",
CARESU-COV-0485,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.3,"Benefit: Cumulative Bonus Insured by 50% flat, on a cumulative basis, as a Cumulative Bonus for each completed and continuous Policy Year, and subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit: Cumulative Bonus Insured by 50% flat, on a cumulative basis, as a Cumulative Bonus for each completed and continuous Policy Year, and subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARESU-EXC-0486,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.3(i),"In any Policy Year, the accrued Cumulative Bonus, shall not exceed 100% of the Sum Insured available in the expiring Policy or renewed Policy, wherever Sum Insured is lower.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0487,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.3(iv),"If the Insured Persons in the expiring policy are covered on Individual basis and thus have accumulated the Cumulative Bonus for each Insured Person in the expiring policy, and such expiring policy is renewed with the Company on a Floater basis, then the Cumulative Bonus to be carried forward for credit in this Policy would be the least Cumulative Bonus amongst all the Insured Persons.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0488,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.3(v),"If the Insured Persons in the expiring policy are covered on a Floater basis and such Insured Persons renew their expiring Policy with the Company by splitting the Floater Sum Insured in to 2 (two) or more Individual/ Floater covers, then the Cumulative Bonus of the expiring Policy shall be apportioned to such renewed Policy in the proportion of the Sum Insured of each of the renewed Policy.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0489,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.3(ix),The 'Unlimited Automatic Recharge' and Optional Benefit: 'Plus Benefit' amount shall not be considered while calculating 'Cumulative Bonus'.,EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0490,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.3(x),"Accrued 'Cumulative Bonus' can be utilized for Base Benefits- 'Hospitalization Expenses', ' Road Ambulance Cover' under the (xi) Cumulative Bonus would be credited automatically to the subsequent Policy year, even in case of multi-year Policies (with 2 or 3 year policy t tenure).",COVERAGE,False,,3 years
CARESU-COV-0491,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.4,"Benefit : Unlimited Automatic Recharge If a Claim is payable under the Policy, then the Company agrees to automatically make the re-instatement of up to the base Sum Insured unlimited times in a policy year which is valid for that Policy Year only, subject to the conditions specified below:",COVERAGE,True,"Benefit : Unlimited Automatic Recharge If a Claim is payable under the Policy, then the Company agrees to automatically make the re-instatement of up to the base Sum Insured unlimited times in a policy year which is valid for that Policy Year only, subject to the conditions specified below:",
CARESU-COV-0492,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.4(i),"The Recharge shall be utilized only after the base Sum Insured, applicable Cumulative Bonus , Cumulative Bonus Super (if applicable) and Plus Benefit (if applicable) have been completely exhausted in that Policy Year.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0493,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.4(ii),A Claim will be admissible under the Recharge only if the Claim is admissible under Benefit 'Hospitalization Expenses'.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0494,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.4(iv),The Sum Insured available under this Benefit can only be utilized for Benefits – 'Hospitalization Expenses' and 'Road Ambulance Cover'.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0495,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.4(v),All Insured Persons will be eligible to utilize the Recharged amount for any illness or injury pertaining to that Policy Year.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0496,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.4(vi),"Applicable 'Cumulative Bonus ' ,'Optional Benefit: Cumulative Bonus Super' , Optional Benefit: Plus Benefit shall not be considered while calculating 'Unlimited Automatic Recharge'.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0497,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.5,Benefit : Unlimited E-Consultation The Company shall offer unlimited e-consultations with qualified General Physicians at our network during the Policy Year through any mode of communication as available (Voice/Video Call /Chat /Email Chat/etc.),COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0498,Care Health,Care Supreme,2.2. Specific Definitions,3.1.6,Benefit: Health Services The Company shall provide the following Services:,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0499,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,3.2.1,"Smart Select If this Optional Benefit is opted, then Policyholder is entitled for a reduction in the total premium (which includes premium of Base Benefits, Optional Benefits- Room Rent Modification, PED Wait Period Modification, Named Ailment Wait Period Modification, Instant Cover, Deductible, Co-payment, New Born Cover, Plus Benefit, Cumulative Bonus Super, Air Ambulance cover, Unlimited Care) payable as specified in the Policy Schedule, subject to following conditions:",COVERAGE,True,"Smart Select If this Optional Benefit is opted, then Policyholder is entitled for a reduction in the total premium (which includes premium of Base Benefits, Optional Benefits- Room Rent Modification, PED Wait Period Modification, Named Ailment Wait Period Modification, Instant Cover, Deductible, Co-payment, New Born Cover, Plus Benefit, Cumulative Bonus Super, Air Ambulance cover, Unlimited Care) payable as specified in the Policy Schedule, subject to following conditions:",
CARESU-COV-0500,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,3.2.2,"Room Rent Modification Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in the Policy, if this Optional Benefit is opted, the Company agrees to modify the Room Rent / Room Category to Single Private AC room / Twin sharing room as specified in Policy schedule. If the Insured Person is admitted in a Hospital room where the Room Category opted or Room Rent incurred is higher than the eligible Room Category/ Room Rent as specified in the Policy Schedule, then, the Policyholder/Insured Person shall bear the ratable proportion of the total Associate Medical Expenses (including applicable surcharge and taxes thereon) in the proportion of the difference between the Room Rent actually incurred and the Room Rent specified in the Policy Schedule or the Room Rent of the entitled Room Category to the Room Rent actually incurred.",COVERAGE,True,"Room Rent Modification Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in the Policy, if this Optional Benefit is opted, the Company agrees to modify the Room Rent / Room Category to Single Private AC room / Twin sharing room as specified in Policy schedule.",
CARESU-COV-0501,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,3.2.2(i),"Single Private AC Room If the Policy Schedule states 'Single Private AC Room' as eligible Room Category, it means the maximum eligible Room Category in case of Hospitalization of the Insured Person payable by the Company is limited for stay in a Single Private AC Room.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0502,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,3.2.2(ii),"Twin Sharing Room If the Policy Schedule states 'Twin Sharing Room' as eligible Room Category, it means the maximum eligible Room Category in case of Hospitalization of the Insured Person payable by the Company is limited for stay in a Twin Sharing Room .",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-DEF-0503,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,1,"The nomenclature of Room categories may vary from one hospital to the other. Hence, the final consideration will be as per the definition of the Rooms mentioned in the Policy.",DEFINITION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0504,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,2,No limit on ICU charges under this Optional Benefit.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-WAI-0505,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,3.2.3,"PED Wait Period Modification Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in the Policy, by choosing this Optional Benefit, the applicable waiting period of 36 months for Claims related to Pre-existing diseases shall be modified to specific time period as mentioned in the Policy Schedule.",WAITING_PERIOD,True,"PED Wait Period Modification Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in the Policy, by choosing this Optional Benefit, the applicable waiting period of 36 months for Claims related to Pre-existing diseases shall be modified to specific time period as mentioned in the Policy Schedule.",36 months
CARESU-WAI-0506,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,3.2.3,"Hence all the provisions stated under Clause 4.1 (a) (i) and Definition 2.1.36 holds good for this benefit as well, except that the claims will be admissible for any Medical Expenses incurred for Hospitalization in respect of diagnosis/treatment of any Pre Existing Disease after specific time period of continuous coverage has elapsed as mentioned in the Policy Schedule, since the inception of the first Policy with the Company.",WAITING_PERIOD,True,"Hence all the provisions stated under Clause 4.1 (a) (i) and Definition 2.1.36 holds good for this benefit as well, except that the claims will be admissible for any Medical Expenses incurred for Hospitalization in respect of diagnosis/treatment of any Pre Existing Disease after specific time period of continuous coverage has elapsed as mentioned in the Policy Schedule, since the inception of the first Policy with the Company.",
CARESU-WAI-0507,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,3.2.4,"Named Ailment Wait Period Modification Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in the Policy, by choosing this Optional Benefit, the applicable waiting period of 24 months for Claims related to Names ailments shall be modified to specific time period as mentioned in the Policy Schedule. Hence, all the provisions stated under Clause 4.1 (a) (ii) holds good for this benefit as well, except that the claims will be admissible for any Medical Expenses incurred for Hospitalization in respect of diagnosis/treatment of any Named ailment Disease after specific time period of continuous coverage has elapsed as mentioned in the Policy Schedule, since the inception of the first Policy with the Company.",WAITING_PERIOD,True,"Named Ailment Wait Period Modification Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in the Policy, by choosing this Optional Benefit, the applicable waiting period of 24 months for Claims related to Names ailments shall be modified to specific time period as mentioned in the Policy Schedule.",24 months
CARESU-WAI-0508,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,3.2.5,"Instant Cover Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in the Policy, by choosing this Optional Benefit the Company shall waive off the applicable PED waiting period on Diabetes/ Hypertension/ Hyperlipidemia/ Asthma at the time of issuance of first Policy with the Company and coverage shall start from the 31st day of Policy start date after serving Initial wait period of 30 days.",WAITING_PERIOD,True,"Instant Cover Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in the Policy, by choosing this Optional Benefit the Company shall waive off the applicable PED waiting period on Diabetes/ Hypertension/ Hyperlipidemia/ Asthma at the time of issuance of first Policy with the Company and coverage shall start from the 31st day of Policy start date after serving Initial wait period of 30 days.",30 days
CARESU-COV-0509,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,3.2.5(i),The above Optional Benefit can be opted only if this policy is issued for the first time with the Company and on continues renewal without break in policy.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0510,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,3.2.5(ii),Either Optional Benefit - 'Instant Cover' or 'PED Wait Period Modification' can be opted but not both.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0511,Care Health,Care Supreme,3.2. Optional Benefits,3.2.6,"Deductible If this Optional Benefit is opted, then Policyholder is entitled for a discount on the Premium payable.",COVERAGE,False,,
