CARESU-COV-0612,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.2(a),"Cashless Facility The Company extends Cashless Facility as a mode to indemnify the medical expenses incurred by the Insured Person at a Network Provider. For this purpose, the Insured Person will be issued a “Health card” at the time of Policy purchase, which has to be preserved and produced at any of the Network Providers in the event of Claim being made, to avail Cashless Facility. The following is the process for availing Cashless Facility:-.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-EXC-0613,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.2(a),"If the request for availing Cashless Facility is authorized by the Company, then payment for the Medical Expenses incurred in respect of the Insured Person shall not have to be made to the extent that such Medical Expenses are covered under this Policy and fall within the amount authorized in writing by the Company for availing Cashless Facility.",EXCLUSION,False,,
CARESU-COV-0614,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.2(vi),"Company's Rejection: If the Company does not authorize the Cashless Facility due to insufficient Sum Insured or insufficient information provided to the Company to determine the admissibility of the Claim, then payment for such treatment will have to be made by the Policyholder / Insured Person to the Network Provider, following which a Claim for reimbursement may be made to the Company which shall be considered subject to the Insured Person's Policy limits and relevant conditions. Please note that rejection of a Pre-authorization request is in no way construed as rejection of coverage or treatment. The Insured Person can proceed with the treatment, settle the hospital bills and submit the claim for a possible reimbursement.",COVERAGE,True,"Company's Rejection: If the Company does not authorize the Cashless Facility due to insufficient Sum Insured or insufficient information provided to the Company to determine the admissibility of the Claim, then payment for such treatment will have to be made by the Policyholder / Insured Person to the Network Provider, following which a Claim for reimbursement may be made to the Company which shall be considered subject to the Insured Person's Policy limits and relevant conditions.",
CARESU-WAI-0615,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.2(i),"It is agreed and understood that in all cases where intimation of a Claim has been provided under Reimbursement Facility and/or the Company specifically states that a particular Benefit is payable only under Reimbursement Facility, all the information and documentation specified in Clause 6.1.4 and Clause 6.1.5 shall be submitted to the Company at Policyholder's / Insured Person's own expense, immediately and in any event within 30 days of Insured Person's discharge from Hospital.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
CARESU-COV-0616,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.2(iii),"In case a reimbursement claim is received after a Pre- Authorization letter has been issued for the same case earlier, before processing such claim, a check will be made with the Network Provider whether the Pre-authorization has been utilized. Once such check and declaration is received from the Network Provider, the case will be processed.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0617,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.2(iv),"For Claim settlement under reimbursement, the Company will pay the Policyholder. In the event of death of the Policyholder, the Company will pay the nominee (as named in the Policy Schedule) and in case of no nominee, to the legal heirs or legal representatives of the Policyholder whose discharge shall be treated as full and final discharge of its liability under the Policy.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0618,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.2(v),Date of Loss' under Reimbursement Facility is the 'Date of Admission' to Hospital in case of Hospitalization & actual Date of Loss for non-Hospitalization related Benefits.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0619,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.4(i),"If any Illness is diagnosed or discovered or any Injury is suffered or any other contingency occurs which has resulted in a Claim or may result in a Claim under the Policy, the Company shall be notified with full particulars within 48 hours from the date of occurrence of event either at the Company's call center or in writing.",COVERAGE,False,,48 hours
CARESU-WAI-0620,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.4(ii),Claim must be filed within 30 days from the date of discharge from the hospital in case of hospitalization and actual date of loss in case of non-hospitalization Benefits.,WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
CARESU-COV-0621,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,13,- Additional documents as specified against any Benefit shall be submitted to the company.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0622,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.6(i),"If a room accommodation has been opted for where the Room Rent or Room Category is higher than the eligible limit as applicable for that Insured Person as specified in the Policy Schedule, then, the Associate Medical Expenses payable shall be pro-rated as per the applicable limits in accordance with Clause 3.1.1(ix) and 3.2.2.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0623,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.6(ii),The Deductible (if applicable) shall be applied to the aggregate of all Claims that are either paid or payable under this Policy. The Company's liability to make payment shall commence only once the aggregate amount of all Claims payable or paid exceed the Deductible.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0624,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.6(iii),Co-payment (if applicable) shall be applicable on the admissible claim amount payable by the Company.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0625,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.6(iv),"The balance amount, if any, subject to the applicability of sub- limits, Company's liability to make payment shall be limited to such extent as applicable and shall be the Claim payable c. The Claim amount assessed in Clause 6.1.6 (b) above would be deducted from the following amounts in the following progressive order:",COVERAGE,True,"The balance amount, if any, subject to the applicability of sub- limits, Company's liability to make payment shall be limited to such extent as applicable and shall be the Claim payable c.",
CARESU-COV-0626,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.6(ii),"Plus benefit , as applicable (iii) Cumulative Bonus (iv) Cumulative Bonus Super , as applicable.",COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0627,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.6(a),This Policy covers only medical treatment taken entirely within India. All payments under this Policy shall be made in Indian Rupees and within India.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0628,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.6(f),The Policy covers Reasonable and Customary Charges incurred towards medical treatment taken or any other expenses triggers under a any Benefit during the Policy Period.,COVERAGE,False,,
CARESU-COV-0629,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.6(g),"Under this Policy, the Company's total, cumulative, maximum liability during the Policy Year is maximum up to the Sum Insured unless any additional Sum Insured available or accrued under any Benefit.",COVERAGE,True,"Under this Policy, the Company's total, cumulative, maximum liability during the Policy Year is maximum up to the Sum Insured unless any additional Sum Insured available or accrued under any Benefit.",
CARESU-COV-0630,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.6(h),"For diseases or conditions or procedure that have a specified sub-limit then all related expenses shall be covered up to the sub-limit specified for that disease or condition or procedure. In case there is a specified sub-limit then the Company's total, cumulative, maximum liability during the Policy Year is maximum up to the specified sub-limit subject to the available Sum Insured in the Policy Year.",COVERAGE,True,"In case there is a specified sub-limit then the Company's total, cumulative, maximum liability during the Policy Year is maximum up to the specified sub-limit subject to the available Sum Insured in the Policy Year.",
CARESU-COV-0631,Care Health,Care Supreme,5. General Terms And Clauses,6.1.6,"For example- if the Policy specifies a sub-limit of Rs. 50,000 for a particular disease then all expenses related to the treatment of that disease (including but not limited to pre-hospitalization, hospitalization and post- hospitalization) will be covered up to Rs. 50,000, subject to Sum Insured availability in the Policy Year even if the overall Sum Insured is higher.",COVERAGE,True,"For example- if the Policy specifies a sub-limit of Rs. 50,000 for a particular disease then all expenses related to the treatment of that disease (including but not limited to pre-hospitalization, hospitalization and post- hospitalization) will be covered up to Rs. 50,000, subject to Sum Insured availability in the Policy Year even if the overall Sum Insured is higher.",
