OPTIMA-EXC-0648,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,General,,"HDFC ERGO General Insurance Company Limited will cover all the Insured Persons under this Policy upto the Sum Insured. The insurance cover is governed by, and subject to, the terms, conditions and exclusions of this Policy.",EXCLUSION,True,"The insurance cover is governed by, and subject to, the terms, conditions and exclusions of this Policy.",
OPTIMA-DEF-0649,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,General,,"SECTION A. DEFINITIONS: OTHER IMPORTANT TERMS YOU SHOULD KNOW The terms defined below and at other junctures in the Policy Wording have the meanings ascribed to them wherever they appear in this Policy and, where appropriate, references to the singular include references to the plural; references to the male include the female and references to any statutory enactment include subsequent changes to the same:",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0650,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 1,"Accident means a sudden, unforeseen and involuntary event caused by external, visible and violent means.",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0651,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 2,Any one illness means continuous Period of illness and it includes relapse within 45 days from the date of last consultation with the Hospital/Nursing Home where treatment was been taken.,DEFINITION,False,,45 days
OPTIMA-DEF-0652,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 4,"AYUSH Day Care Centre means and includes Community Health Centre (CHC), Primary Health Centre (PHC), Dispensary, Clinic, Polyclinic or any such health centre which is registered with the local authorities, wherever applicable and having facilities for carrying out treatment procedures and medical or surgical/para-surgical interventions or both under the supervision of registered AYUSH Medical Practitioner(s) on day care basis without in-patient services and must comply with all the following criterion:",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0653,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 5,"Cashless facility means a facility extended by the insurer to the insured where the payments, of the costs of treatment undergone by the insured in accordance with the policy terms and conditions, are directly made to the network provider by the insurer to the extent pre-authorization approved.",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0654,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 6,Condition Precedent means a policy term or condition upon which the Insurer’s liability under the policy is conditional upon.,DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0655,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 7,"Congenital Anomaly refers to a condition(s) which is present since birth, and which is abnormal with reference to form, structure or position.",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0656,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 8,Co-payment means a cost-sharing requirement under a health insurance policy that provides that the policyholder/insured will bear a specified percentage of the admissible claim amount. A co-payment does not reduce the Sum Insured.,DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-COV-0657,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 9,Cumulative Bonus (Multiplier Benefit) means any increase in the Sum Insured granted by the insurer without an associated increase in premium.,COVERAGE,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0658,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 10,"Critical Illness means Cancer of specified severity, Open Chest CABG, First Heart Attack of specified severity, Kidney Failure requiring regular dialysis, Major Organ/Bone Marrow Transplant, Multiple Sclerosis with Persisting Symptoms, Permanent Paralysis of Limbs, Stroke resulting in Permanent Symptoms as defined below only:",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-EXC-0659,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 10,"The actual undergoing of open chest surgery for the correction of one or more coronary arteries, which is/are narrowed or blocked, by coronary artery bypass graft (CABG). The Diagnosis must be supported by coronary angiography and realisation of the surgery has to be confirmed by a specialist Medical Practitioner The following are excluded:",EXCLUSION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0660,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 10,The first occurrence of myocardial infarction which means the death of a portion of the heart muscle as a result of inadequate blood supply to the relevant area.,DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-EXC-0661,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 10,▪ Neurological damage due to SLE is excluded.,EXCLUSION,False,,
OPTIMA-COV-0662,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 10,Total and irreversible loss of use of two or more limbs as a result of injury or disease of the brain or spinal cord. A specialist Medical Practitioner (Physician / Neurologist) must be of the opinion that paralysis will be permanent with no hope of recovery and must be present for more than 3 months.,COVERAGE,False,,3 months
OPTIMA-DEF-0663,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 11,"Day Care centre means any institution established for day care treatment of illness and/or injuries or a medical setup within a hospital and which has been registered with the local authorities, wherever applicable, and is under the supervision of a registered and qualified medical practitioner AND must comply with all minimum criteria as under— - has qualified nursing staff under its employment;",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0664,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 12,"Day Care Procedures means those medical treatment, and/or surgical procedure.",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0665,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 12,Treatment normally taken on an Out-patient basis is not included in the scope of this definition.,DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-COV-0666,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 13,Deductible means a cost-sharing requirement under a health insurance policy that provides that the insurer will not be liable for a specified rupee amount in case of indemnity policies and for a specified number of days/hours in case of hospital cash policies which will apply before any benefits are payable by the insurer. A deductible does not reduce the Sum Insured.,COVERAGE,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0667,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 14,"Dental treatment means a treatment related to teeth or structures supporting teeth including examinations, filings (where appropriate), crowns, extractions and surgery.",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0668,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 16,"Disclosure of information norm means the policy shall be void and all premiums paid hereon shall be forfeited to the Company, in the event of misrepresentation, mis-description or non- disclosure of any material fact.",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0669,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 17,"Emergency Care means management for a severe illness or injury which results in symptoms which occur suddenly and unexpectedly, and requires immediate care by a medical practitioner to prevent death or serious long term impairment of the insured person’s health.",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-EXC-0670,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 18,"Grace Period means the specified period of time, immediately following the premium due date during which premium payment can be made to renew or continue a policy in force without loss of continuity benefits pertaining to waiting periods and coverage of pre-existing diseases. Coverage need not be available during the period for which no premium is received. The grace period for payment of the premium for all types of insurance policies shall be: fifteen days where premium payment mode is monthly and thirty days in all other cases. Provided the insurers shall offer coverage during the grace period, if the premium is paid in instalments during the policy period (Note: In case of non-instalment premium payment, coverage shall not be available for the period for which no premium is received).",EXCLUSION,False,,30 days
OPTIMA-DEF-0671,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 19,"Hospital means any institution established for in-patient care and day care treatment of illness and/or injuries and which has been registered as a hospital with the local authorities under the Clinical Establishments (Registration and Regulation) Act, 2010 or under the enactments specified under the Schedule of Section 56(1) of the said Act OR complies with all minimum criteria as under:",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0672,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 20,"Hospitalisation means admission in a Hospital for a minimum of 24 consecutive ‘In-patient Care’ hours except for specified procedures / treatments, where such admission could be for a period of less than 24 consecutive hours.",DEFINITION,True,"Hospitalisation means admission in a Hospital for a minimum of 24 consecutive ‘In-patient Care’ hours except for specified procedures / treatments, where such admission could be for a period of less than 24 consecutive hours.",24 hours
OPTIMA-DEF-0673,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 21,Illness means a sickness or a disease or pathological condition leading to the impairment of normal physiological function and requires medical treatment.,DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-COV-0674,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 21(a),"Acute Condition- Acute condition is a disease, illness or injury that is likely to respond quickly to treatment which aims to return the person to his or her state of health immediately before suffering the disease/illness/injury which leads to full recovery.",COVERAGE,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0675,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 21(b),"Chronic Condition- A chronic condition is defined as disease, illness, or injury that has one or more of the following characteristics:",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0676,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 22,"Injury means accidental physical bodily harm excluding illness or disease solely and directly caused by external, violent and visible and evident means which is verified and certified by a Medical Practitioner.",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-COV-0677,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 23,In-patient Care means treatment for which the Insured Person has to stay in a Hospital for more than 24 hours for a covered event.,COVERAGE,False,,24 hours
OPTIMA-DEF-0678,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 24,"Intensive Care Unit means an identified section, ward or wing of a Hospital which is under the constant supervision of a dedicated Medical Practitioner(s), and which is specially equipped for the continuous monitoring and treatment of patients who are in a critical condition, or require life support facilities and where the level of care and supervision is considerably more sophisticated and intensive than in the ordinary and other wards.",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-COV-0679,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 25,"ICU (Intensive Care Unit) Charges means the amount charged by a Hospital towards ICU expenses which shall include the coverage for bed, general medical support services provided to any ICU patient including monitoring devices, critical care nursing and intensive charges.",COVERAGE,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0680,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 27,Medical Advice means any consultation or advise from a Medical Practitioner including the issue of any prescription or repeat prescription.,DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-COV-0681,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 28,"Medical Expenses means those expenses that an Insured Person has necessarily and actually incurred for medical treatment on account of illness or Accident on the advice of a Medical Practitioner, as long as these are no more than would have been payable if the Insured Person had not been insured and no more than other Hospitals or doctors in the same locality would have charged for the same medical treatment.",COVERAGE,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0682,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 29,"Medically Necessary Treatment means any treatment, test, medication, or stay in Hospital or.",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0683,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 30,Medical Practitioner means a person who holds a valid registration from the medical council of any state or medical council of India or council for Indian medicine or for homeopathy set up by the government of India or a state government and is thereby entitled to practice medicine within its jurisdiction; and is acting within the scope and jurisdiction of license.,DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-WAI-0684,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 31,"Migration means a facility provided to policyholders (including all members under family cover and group policies), to transfer the credits gained for pre-existing diseases and specific waiting periods from one health insurance policy to another with the same insurer.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0685,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 32,Network Provider means Hospital enlisted by an insurer or a TPA or jointly by an insurer and a TPA to provide medical services to an insured by a cashless facility.,DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0686,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 33,New Born Baby means baby born during the Policy Period and is aged up to 90 days.,DEFINITION,False,,90 days
OPTIMA-DEF-0687,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 34,"Non-Network Provider means any Hospital, day care centre or other provider that is not part of the Network.",DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0688,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 35,Notification of Claim means the process of intimating a claim to the insurer or TPA through any of the recognized modes of communication.,DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-DEF-0689,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 36,OPD treatment means the one in which the Insured visits a clinic / hospital or associated facility like a consultation room for diagnosis and treatment based on the advice of a Medical Practitioner. The Insured is not admitted as a day care or in-patient.,DEFINITION,False,,
OPTIMA-WAI-0690,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 37,"Portability means a facility provided to the health insurance policyholders (including all members under family cover), to transfer the credits gained for, pre-existing diseases and specific waiting periods from one insurer to another insurer.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
OPTIMA-WAI-0691,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 38,"Pre-existing Disease means any condition, ailment, injury or disease:",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
OPTIMA-WAI-0692,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 38,"that is/are diagnosed by a physician not more than 36 months prior to the date of commencement of the policy issued by the insurer; or for which medical advice or treatment was recommended by, or received from, a physician, not more than 36 months prior to the date of commencement of the policy.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,36 months
OPTIMA-DEF-0693,HDFC ERGO,Optima Restore,1. Standard Definition,Def. 39,"Pre- Hospitalisation Medical Expenses means the medical expenses incurred during predefined number of days preceding the hospitalization of the Insured Person, provided that:",DEFINITION,True,"Pre- Hospitalisation Medical Expenses means the medical expenses incurred during predefined number of days preceding the hospitalization of the Insured Person, provided that:",
