STARCO-COV-2641,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,2,"Note: For assistance call 24 hours help- line 044-69006900 or Toll Free No. 1800 425 2255, Senior Citizens may call at 044-40020888 For the comprehensive list of documents to be submitted while filing a reimbursement claim, please refer our website under the link https://www. starhealth.in/claims/#claim-process F. Claims of Out Patient Consultations / treatments will be settled on cashless basis.",COVERAGE,False,,24 hours
STARCO-COV-2642,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,2,"H. Following an admissible claim under Section II.23, the coverage under Personal Accident insurance upon renewal will be applicable for the person to be chosen by the Proposer at the time of renewal, subject to other terms, conditions contained herein.",COVERAGE,True,"Following an admissible claim under Section II.23, the coverage under Personal Accident insurance upon renewal will be applicable for the person to be chosen by the Proposer at the time of renewal, subject to other terms, conditions contained herein.",
STARCO-COV-2643,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,3,"Complete Discharge: Any payment to the policyholder, Insured Person or his/ her nominees or his/ her legal representative or assignee or to the Hospital, as the case may be, for any benefit under the policy shall be a valid discharge towards payment of claim by the Company to the extent of that amount for the particular claim.",COVERAGE,False,,
STARCO-COV-2644,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,4(i),"ln case of multiple policies taken by an Insured Person during a period from one or more insurers to indemnify treatment costs, the Insured Person shall have the right to require a settlement of his/her claim in terms of any of his/her policies. ln all such cases the insurer chosen by the Insured Person shall be obliged to settle the claim as long as the claim is within the limits of and according to the terms of the chosen policy.",COVERAGE,False,,
STARCO-COV-2645,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,4(iv),"Where an Insured Person has policies from more than one insurer to cover the same risk on indemnity basis, the Insured Person shall only be indemnified the treatment costs in accordance with the terms and conditions of the chosen policy Applicable for Sections II.22 and II.23 In case of multiple policies which provide fixed benefits, on the occurrence of the insured event, each insurer shall make the claim payments independent of payments received under other similar polices in accordance with the terms and conditions of the policies.",COVERAGE,False,,
STARCO-COV-2646,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,4,The Policyholder is expected to disclose all the health insurance policies under which the lives proposed for insurance are covered.,COVERAGE,False,,
STARCO-COV-2647,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,5,"Fraud: lf any claim made by the Insured Person, is in any respect fraudulent, or if any false statement, or declaration is made or used in support thereof, or if any fraudulent means or devices are used by the Insured Person or anyone acting on his/her behalf to obtain any benefit under this policy, all benefits under this policy and the premium paid shall be forfeited.",COVERAGE,False,,
STARCO-DEF-2648,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,5,"For the purpose of this clause, the expression “fraud” means any of the following acts committed by the Insured Person or by his agent or the hospital/ doctor/any other party acting on behalf of the Insured Person, with intent to deceive the insurer or to induce the insurer to issue an insurance policy:",DEFINITION,False,,
STARCO-EXC-2649,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,5(iv),"any such act or omission as the law specially declares to be fraudulent The Company shall not repudiate the claim and / or forfeit the policy benefits on the ground of Fraud, if the Insured Person / beneficiary can prove that the misstatement was true to the best of his knowledge and there was no deliberate intention to suppress the fact or that such misstatement of or suppression of material fact are within the knowledge of the insurer.",EXCLUSION,False,,
STARCO-COV-2650,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,5,"b. refund premium for the unexpired Policy Period, in respect of policies with Policy Term more than 1 year and risk coverage for such Policy Years has not commenced.",COVERAGE,False,,1 year
STARCO-WAI-2651,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,7,"Migration: In case of migration of one policy to another with the same insurer, the Policyholder (including all members under family cover and group insurance policies) can transfer the credits gained to the extent of the Sum Insured, No Claim Bonus, Specific Waiting Periods, Waiting period for Pre-Existing Diseases, Moratorium period etc. in the previous policy to the migrated policy.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
STARCO-WAI-2652,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,7(i),"The Policyholder has the choice to port his / her policy from one Insurer to another by applying to such Insurer to port the entire policy along with all the members of the family, if any, at least 30 days before, but not earlier than 60 days from the policy renewal date as per IRDAI guidelines related to portability.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days; 60 days
STARCO-WAI-2653,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,7(ii),"The Policyholder is entitled to transfer the credits gained to the extent of the Sum Insured, No Claim Bonus, Specific Waiting Periods, Waiting period for Pre-Existing Diseases, Moratorium period etc. from the existing Insurer to the Acquiring Insurer in the previous policy.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
STARCO-WAI-2654,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,9(i),"At the end of the Policy Period, the policy shall terminate and can be renewed within the Grace Period of 30 days.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
STARCO-WAI-2655,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,9(ii),"While coverage is not available during the Grace Period, if the policy is renewed during the Grace Period, all the credits (Sum Insured, No Claim Bonus, Specific Waiting Periods, Waiting period for Pre- Existing Diseases, Moratorium period etc.) accrued under the policy shall be protected.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
STARCO-WAI-2656,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,10(ii),"Policyholder will have the option to migrate to similar health insurance product available with the Company at the time of renewal. Policyholder can transfer the credits gained (to the extent of Sum Insured, No Claim Bonus, Specific Waiting Periods, Waiting period for Pre-Existing Diseases, Moratorium period etc.) in the previous policy to the migrated policy, provided the policy has been maintained without a break.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
STARCO-WAI-2657,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,11,Moratorium Period: After completion of sixty continuous months of coverage (including portability and migration),WAITING_PERIOD,False,,60 months
STARCO-WAI-2658,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,11,"in health insurance policy, no policy and claim shall be contestable by the insurer on grounds of non-disclosure, misrepresentation, except on grounds of established fraud. This period of sixty continuous months is called as moratorium period. The moratorium would be applicable for the Sums Insured of the first policy. Wherever, the Sum Insured is enhanced, completion of sixty continuous months would be applicable from the date of enhancement of Sums Insured only on the enhanced limits.",WAITING_PERIOD,True,"in health insurance policy, no policy and claim shall be contestable by the insurer on grounds of non-disclosure, misrepresentation, except on grounds of established fraud.",60 months
STARCO-WAI-2659,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,12(ii),"For Quarterly, Half yearly and Yearly instalment option: Grace Period of 30 days would be given to pay the instalment premium due for the policy.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
STARCO-WAI-2660,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,12(iii),"The Policyholder will get the accrued continuity benefit in respect of the (Sum Insured, No Claim Bonus, Specific Waiting Periods, Waiting period for Pre-Existing Diseases, Moratorium period etc.) in the event of payment of premium within the stipulated Grace Period.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
STARCO-COV-2661,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,12(vi),"ln the event of a claim, all subsequent premium instalments shall immediately become due and payable.",COVERAGE,False,,
STARCO-COV-2662,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,12(vii),The company has the right to recover and deduct all the pending instalments from the claim amount due under the policy.,COVERAGE,False,,
STARCO-COV-2663,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,12(viii),"For premium paid in instalments during the Policy Period, coverage is available during the Grace Period also.",COVERAGE,False,,
STARCO-COV-2664,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,14,"The Policyholder shall be entitled to a refund of the premium paid subject only to a deduction of a proportionate risk premium for the period of cover and the expenses, if any incurred by the Insurer on medical examination of the proposer and stamp duty charges.",COVERAGE,False,,
STARCO-COV-2665,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,18,All claims under this policy shall be payable in Indian currency.,COVERAGE,False,,
STARCO-COV-2666,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,19,"The premium payable under this policy shall be payable in advance. No receipt of premium shall be valid except on the official form of the company signed by a duly authorized official of the company. The due payment of premium and the observance of fulfillment of the terms, provision, conditions and endorsements of this policy by the Insured Person/s, in so far as they relate to anything to be done or complied with by the Insured Person/s, shall be a condition precedent to any liability of the Company to make any payment under this policy. No waiver of any terms, provisions, conditions, and endorsements of this policy shall be valid unless made in writing and signed by an authorized official of the Company.",COVERAGE,True,No receipt of premium shall be valid except on the official form of the company signed by a duly authorized official of the company.,
STARCO-COV-2667,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,23(i),"Upon the death of the Insured Person. This also means that in case of family floater policy, cover for the other surviving members of the family will continue, subject to other terms of the policy.",COVERAGE,True,"This also means that in case of family floater policy, cover for the other surviving members of the family will continue, subject to other terms of the policy.",
STARCO-COV-2668,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,23(ii),Upon exhaustion of the Limit of Coverage.,COVERAGE,False,,
STARCO-EXC-2669,Star Health,Star Comprehensive,General,24,"Policy disputes: Any dispute concerning the interpretation of the terms, conditions, limitations and/or exclusions contained herein is understood and agreed to by both the Insured and the Company to be subject to Indian Law.",EXCLUSION,True,"Policy disputes: Any dispute concerning the interpretation of the terms, conditions, limitations and/or exclusions contained herein is understood and agreed to by both the Insured and the Company to be subject to Indian Law.",
