FAMILY-DEF-2682,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Accident: An accident means sudden, unforeseen and involuntary event caused by external, visible and violent means.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2683,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Any one illness: Any one illness means continuous period of illness and includes relapse within 45 days from the date of last consultation with the Hospital/Nursing Home where treatment was taken.,DEFINITION,False,,45 days
FAMILY-DEF-2684,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"AYUSH Day Care Centre: AYUSH Day Care Centre means and includes Community Health Centre (CHC), Primary Health Centre (PHC), Dispensary, Clinic, Polyclinic or any such health centre which is registered with the local authorities, wherever applicable and having facilities for carrying out treatment procedures and medical or surgical/ para-surgical interventions or both under the supervision of registered AYUSH Medical Practitioner (s) on day care basis without in-patient services and must comply with all the following criterion:",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2685,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"AYUSH Treatment: AYUSH treatment refers to the medical and / or hospitalization treatments given under ‘Ayurveda, Yoga and Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha and Homeopathy systems’.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2686,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Break in policy: Break in policy means the period of gap that occurs at the end of the existing Policy Term/instalment premium due date, when the premium due for renewal on a given policy or instalment premium due is not paid on or before the premium renewal date or grace period.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2687,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Cashless facility: Cashless facility means a facility extended by the insurer to the insured where the payments, of the costs of treatment undergone by the insured in accordance with the Policy Terms and conditions, are directly made to the network provider by the insurer to the extent pre-authorization is approved.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2688,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Condition Precedent: Condition Precedent means a Policy Term or condition upon which the Insurer's liability under the policy is conditional upon.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2689,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Congenital Anomaly: Congenital Anomaly means a condition which is present since birth, and which is abnormal with reference to form, structure or position.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2690,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,External Congenital Anomaly: Congenital anomaly which is in the visible and accessible parts of the body Co-Payment: Co-payment means a cost-sharing requirement under a health insurance policy that provides that the policyholder/insured will bear a specified percentage of the admissible claims amount. A co-payment does not reduce the Sum Insured.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2691,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Day Care Centre: A day care centre means any institution established for day care treatment of illness and/or injuries or a medical setup with a hospital and which has been registered with the local authorities, wherever applicable, and is under supervision of a registered and qualified medical practitioner AND must comply with all minimum criterion as under-.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2692,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Day Care Treatment: Day care treatment means medical treatment, and/or surgical procedure which is:",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2693,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"which would have otherwise required hospitalization of more than 24 hours Treatment normally taken on an out-patient basis is not included in the scope of this deﬁnition Dental Treatment: Dental treatment means a treatment related to teeth or structures supporting teeth including examinations, fillings (where appropriate), crowns, extractions and surgery.",DEFINITION,False,,24 hours
FAMILY-DEF-2694,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Domiciliary Hospitalization: Domiciliary hospitalization means medical treatment for an illness/disease/injury which in the normal course would require care and treatment at a hospital but is actually taken while conﬁned at home under any of the following circumstances:,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-WAI-2695,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"the patient takes treatment at home on account of non-availability of room in a hospital Grace Period: Grace period means the speciﬁed period of time, immediately following the premium due date during which premium payment can be made to renew or continue a policy in force without loss of continuity beneﬁts pertaining to waiting periods and coverage of pre-existing diseases. Coverage need not be available during the period for which no premium is received. The grace period for payment of the premium for all types of insurance policies shall be: ﬁfteen days where premium payment mode is monthly and thirty days in all other cases. Provided the insurers shall offer coverage during the grace period, if the premium is paid in instalments during the Policy Period.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,30 days
FAMILY-DEF-2696,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Hospital: A hospital means any institution established for in-patient care and day care treatment of illness and/or injuries and which has been registered as a hospital with the local authorities under Clinical Establishments (Registration and Regulation) Act 2010 or under enactments speciﬁed under the Schedule of Section 56(1),DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2697,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Hospitalization: Hospitalization means admission in a Hospital for a minimum period of 24 consecutive ‘In-patient Care’ hours except for specified procedures/ treatments, where such admission could be for a period of less than 24 consecutive hours.",DEFINITION,True,"Hospitalization: Hospitalization means admission in a Hospital for a minimum period of 24 consecutive ‘In-patient Care’ hours except for specified procedures/ treatments, where such admission could be for a period of less than 24 consecutive hours.",24 hours
FAMILY-DEF-2698,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Illness: Illness means a sickness or a disease or pathological condition leading to the impairment of normal physiological function and requires medical treatment;,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-COV-2699,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Acute condition - Acute condition is a disease, illness or injury that is likely to respond quickly to treatment which aims to return the person to his or her state of health immediately before suffering the disease/ illness/ injury which leads to full recovery.",COVERAGE,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2700,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Chronic condition - A chronic condition is defined as a disease, illness, or injury that has one or more of the following characteristics;",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2701,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"a. It needs ongoing or long-term monitoring through consultations, examinations, check-ups, and /or tests b. it needs ongoing or long-term control or relief of symptoms c. it requires rehabilitation for the patient or for the patient to be specially trained to cope with it d. it continues indeﬁnitely e. it recurs or is likely to recur Injury: Injury means accidental physical bodily harm excluding illness or disease solely and directly caused by external, violent, visible and evident means which is verified and certified by a Medical Practitioner.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-COV-2702,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Inpatient Care: Inpatient care means treatment for which the Insured Person has to stay in a hospital for more than 24 hours for a covered event.,COVERAGE,False,,24 hours
FAMILY-DEF-2703,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Intensive Care Unit: Intensive care unit means an identified section, ward or wing of a hospital which is under the constant supervision of a dedicated medical practitioner(s), and which is specially equipped for the continuous monitoring and treatment of patients who are in a critical condition, or require life support facilities and where the level of care and supervision is considerably more sophisticated and intensive than in the ordinary and other wards.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2704,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"ICU Charges: ICU (Intensive Care Unit) Charges means the amount charged by a Hospital towards ICU expenses which shall include the expenses for ICU bed, general medical support services provided to any ICU patient including monitoring devices, critical care nursing and intensivist charges.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2705,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Medical Advice: Medical Advice means any consultation or advice from a Medical Practitioner including the issuance of any prescription or follow-up prescription.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-COV-2706,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Medical Expenses: Medical Expenses means those expenses that an Insured Person has necessarily and actually incurred for medical treatment on account of Illness or Accident on the advice of a Medical Practitioner, as long as these are no more than would have been payable if the Insured Person had not been insured and no more than other hospitals or doctors in the same locality would have charged for the same medical treatment.",COVERAGE,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2707,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Medical Practitioner: Medical Practitioner means a person who holds a valid registration from the Medical Council of any State or Medical Council of India or Council for Indian Medicine or for Homeopathy set up by the Government of India or a State Government and is thereby entitled to practice medicine within its jurisdiction; and is acting within its scope and jurisdiction of license.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2708,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Medically Necessary Treatment: Medically necessary treatment means any treatment, tests, medication, or stay in hospital or part of a stay in hospital which:",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-WAI-2709,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Migration: Migration means a facility provided to policyholders (including all members under family cover and group policies), to transfer the credits gained for pre-existing diseases and specific waiting periods from one health insurance policy to another with the same insurer.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2710,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Network Provider: Network Provider means hospitals or health care providers enlisted by an insurer, TPA or jointly by an Insurer and TPA to provide medical services to an insured by a cashless facility.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2711,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,New Born Baby: Newborn baby means baby born during the Policy Period and is aged upto 90 days.,DEFINITION,False,,90 days
FAMILY-DEF-2712,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Non-Network Provider: Non-Network means any hospital, day care centre or other provider that is not part of the network.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2713,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Notiﬁcation of Claim: Notification of claim means the process of intimating a claim to the insurer or TPA through any of the recognized modes of communication.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-WAI-2714,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Pre-Existing Disease: Pre-existing disease (PED) means any condition, ailment, injury or disease:",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
FAMILY-WAI-2715,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,that is/are diagnosed by a physician not more than 36 months prior to the date of commencement of the policy issued by the insurer;,WAITING_PERIOD,False,,36 months
FAMILY-WAI-2716,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"for which medical advice or treatment was recommended by, or received from, a physician, not more than 36 months prior to the date of commencement of the policy.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,36 months
FAMILY-DEF-2717,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses: Pre- hospitalization Medical Expenses means medical expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days preceding the hospitalization of the Insured Person, provided that:",DEFINITION,True,"Pre-hospitalization Medical Expenses: Pre- hospitalization Medical Expenses means medical expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days preceding the hospitalization of the Insured Person, provided that:",
FAMILY-WAI-2718,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"The In-patient Hospitalization claim for such Hospitalization is admissible by the Insurance Company Portability: Portability means a facility provided to the health insurance policyholders (including all members under family cover), to transfer the credits gained for, pre-existing diseases and specific waiting periods from one insurer to another insurer.",WAITING_PERIOD,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2719,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Post-hospitalization Medical Expenses: Post- hospitalization Medical Expenses means medical expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days immediately after the Insured Person is discharged from the hospital provided that:,DEFINITION,True,Post-hospitalization Medical Expenses: Post- hospitalization Medical Expenses means medical expenses incurred during pre-defined number of days immediately after the Insured Person is discharged from the hospital provided that:,
FAMILY-DEF-2720,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Qualiﬁed Nurse: Qualified nurse means a person who holds a valid registration from the Nursing Council of India or the Nursing Council of any state in India.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2721,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Reasonable and Customary Charges: Reasonable and Customary charges means the charges for services or supplies, which are the standard charges for the speciﬁc provider and consistent with the prevailing charges in the geographical area for identical or similar services, taking into account the nature of the illness / injury involved.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-EXC-2722,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Renewal: Renewal means the terms on which the contract of insurance can be renewed on mutual consent with a provision of grace period for treating the renewal continuous for the purpose of gaining credit for pre-existing diseases, time-bound exclusions and for all waiting periods.",EXCLUSION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2723,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Room Rent: Room Rent means the amount charged by a Hospital towards Room and Boarding expenses and shall include the associated medical expenses.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-EXC-2724,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Specific Waiting Period: Specific Waiting Period means a period up to 36 months from the commencement of a health insurance policy during which period specified diseases/ treatments (except due to an Accident) are not covered. On completion of the period, diseases/ treatments shall be covered provided the policy has been continuously renewed without any break.",EXCLUSION,True,Specific Waiting Period: Specific Waiting Period means a period up to 36 months from the commencement of a health insurance policy during which period specified diseases/ treatments (except due to an Accident) are not covered.,36 months
FAMILY-DEF-2725,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Surgery or Surgical Procedure: Surgery or Surgical Procedure means manual and / or operative procedure(s) required for treatment of an illness or injury, correction of deformities and defects, diagnosis and cure of diseases, relief from suffering and prolongation of life, performed in a hospital or day care centre by a medical practitioner Unproven/Experimental treatment: Unproven/ Experimental treatment means the treatment including drug experimental therapy which is not based on established medical practice in India, is treatment experimental or unproven.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2726,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"S P E C I F I C D E F I N I T I O N S Associated medical expenses: Associated Medical Expenses means expenses that shall include the applicable nursing charges, Operation theatre charges, Professional fees of Medical Practitioner including Surgeon/ anaesthetist/ Physician/Specialist of the Hospital where the Insured Person has been admitted and treated and hence Proportionate deduction will be applicable on these items.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-EXC-2727,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Associated Medical Expenses does not include cost of pharmacy and consumables, cost of implants and medical devices and cost of diagnostics, ICU charges and hence proportionate deduction will not be applicable on these items.",EXCLUSION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2728,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Assisted Reproduction Treatment: Assisted reproduction treatment means Intra Uterine Insemination (IUI), Intra-Cytoplasmic Sperm Injection (ICSI), In-Vitro Fertilisation (IVF) and TESA / TESE (Testicular / Epididymal Sperm Aspiration / Extraction).",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2729,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Company / Insurer / We / Us: Company / Insurer / We / Us means Star Health and Allied Insurance Company Limited.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2730,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Dependent Child: Dependent child means a child (natural or legally adopted) who is financially dependent and does not have his / her independent sources of income and not over 25 years.,DEFINITION,False,,25 years
FAMILY-DEF-2731,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Diagnosis: Diagnosis means diagnosis by a registered medical practitioner, supported by clinical, radiological, histological, histo-pathological and laboratory evidence and also surgical evidence wherever applicable, acceptable to the Company.",DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2732,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,"Home: Home means the Insured Person’s place of residence Home Care Treatment: Home Care Treatment means treatment availed by the Insured Person at home, which in normal course would require care and treatment at a hospital but is actually taken at home provided that:",DEFINITION,True,"Home: Home means the Insured Person’s place of residence Home Care Treatment: Home Care Treatment means treatment availed by the Insured Person at home, which in normal course would require care and treatment at a hospital but is actually taken at home provided that:",
FAMILY-DEF-2733,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Daily monitoring chart including records of treatment administered duly signed by the treating doctor are maintained Insured Person: Insured Person means the name/s of persons named in the schedule of the Policy Instalment: Instalment means frequency of Premium amount paid through Monthly / Quarterly / Half-yearly mode by the Policy Holder/ Insured.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2734,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,In-Patient: In-Patient means an Insured Person who is admitted to Hospital and stays there for a minimum period of 24 hours for the sole purpose of receiving treatment.,DEFINITION,False,,24 hours
FAMILY-COV-2735,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Limit of Coverage: Limit of Coverage means Sum Insured plus Loyalty Bonus earned wherever applicable Policy Period/Policy Year: Policy Period / Policy Year means a year following the commencement date and its subsequent annual anniversary.,COVERAGE,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2736,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Policy Term: Policy Term means the period between the commencement date and expiry date specified in the schedule.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2737,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Shared accommodation: Shared accommodation means a room with two or more patient beds in a Network Hospital.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2738,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Single Standard A/C Room: Single standard A/C Room means a single occupancy air-conditioned room with attached wash room and a couch for the attendant. The room may have a television and / or a telephone.,DEFINITION,False,,
FAMILY-EXC-2739,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Such room must be the most economical of all accommodations available in that hospital as single occupancy. This does not include a deluxe room or a suite.,EXCLUSION,False,,
FAMILY-DEF-2740,Star Health,Family Health Optima,STANDARD DEFINITIONS,,Sum Insured: Sum Insured means the Sum Insured Opted for and for which the premium is paid.,DEFINITION,False,,
